<script>
const CFG={endpoint:''};/*CFG*/
const BK={"lessons":[{"pn":4,"title":"Welcome","sub":"How this book makes your ideas grow","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Most IELTS candidates know what they want to say, but their body paragraphs stay short, repeat the same point, or jump from one idea to the next without proof. This book fixes that with one simple, natural system that works for every Writing Task 2 question: the Idea → Explanation → Result → Example chain.","sz":9.3,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"WHAT IS INSIDE","l":["The Blueprint – a four-paragraph essay structure you can use for any topic.","The Idea Engine – how to turn one idea into a full, convincing paragraph.","Grammar Toolkit – when / if / because / as / by / through, result structures, example phrases,","and concession grammar.","12 Exercises – real Task 2 practice: paraphrasing, While-sentences, topic sentences, connectors,","results, examples, error correction, conclusions and full planning.","Idea Bank – 20 topics × 10 ideas = 200 ideas with natural chunks and Uzbek translations","(emotional, mental, physical, social, financial × benefit and drawback).","5 Model Essays – about 300 words each, built only from Idea Bank chunks, with an X-ray of the","structure."]},{"t":"box","h":"YOUR 5-STEP STUDY ROUTINE","l":["1. Learn the blueprint and grammar pages. 2. Drill the exercises. 3. Borrow two ideas from the","Idea Bank for a topic. 4. Build the chain (Idea → Explanation → Result → Example) in the “Build It”","box. 5. Write a full essay and compare it with a model essay."]},{"t":"box","h":"COLOUR CODE USED IN THE BOOK","l":["Blue = benefit / positive idea | Red = drawback / negative idea. In the Idea Bank every idea","has a code such as 7.6 (topic 7, idea 6). Bold words inside a sentence are chunks: learn them as","ready-made blocks."]},{"t":"box","h":"O‘ZBEKCHA IZOH","l":["Bu kitob sizga fikrni kengaytirishni oʻrgatadi. Har bir gʻoya toʻrt bosqichda yoziladi: Gʻoya → Izoh → Natija → Misol.","Bunday abzats band 7+ uchun juda kuchli, chunki har bir fikr isbotlanadi. Har bir gʻoya va ibora (chunk) oʻzbekcha","tarjimasi bilan berilgan."]}]},{"pn":5,"title":"The Blueprint","sub":"One structure, every Task 2 question","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Use this four-paragraph structure for discussion, opinion and advantages / disadvantages questions. In Body 1 you present the opposite side (the view you support less). In Body 2 you give your opinion and explain it in full. 1. Paraphrase the topic. It is a matter of debate whether… / People disagree about whether… INTRO 2. While-sentence (two sides). While some people argue that A, others believe 2–3 sentences ≈50 words that B. 3. Thesis (optional). This essay will discuss both views, although I believe that… Topic sentence + Idea 1. There are several reasons why…, one of which is… BODY 1 Explanation (when / if / because / as / by / through) Opposite side Result (which leads to / thereby + V-ing / As a result,) ≈100 words Example (For example, / For instance, / Take… as an example) Topic sentence + Idea 1. However, I believe / am convinced that… because… BODY 2 Explanation → Result → Example (same chain as Body 1, but fuller and more My opinion ≈100 words personal) CONCLUSION In conclusion, although / even though [opposite side], I firmly believe that 1–2 sentences [my opinion] because [main reason]. ≈35 words","sz":9.3,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"WHY THIS STRUCTURE WORKS","l":["Examiners reward clear progression: each paragraph has one main idea that is developed, not","listed.","Presenting the opposite side first lets you finish on your own opinion, which sounds confident","and memorable.","Two well-developed ideas (about 300–320 words in total) usually score higher than four thin ideas."]},{"t":"box","h":"QUESTION TYPES → SAME BLUEPRINT","l":["Discuss both views and give your opinion: Body 1 = view you support less, Body 2 = your view.","Do advantages outweigh disadvantages? Body 1 = the side that loses, Body 2 = the side that wins.","To what extent do you agree? Body 1 = reasons some disagree, Body 2 = your reasons for agreeing."]}]},{"pn":6,"title":"The Idea Engine","sub":"How one idea becomes a full paragraph","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"IDEA EXPLANATION RESULT EXAMPLE","sz":9.5,"b":true},{"t":"table","head":["What is my point?","Why? How?","So what happens?","Show me."],"rows":[]},{"t":"p","x":"After every idea, ask the three examiner questions: “Why?” → explanation, “So what?” → result, “For example?” → example. A paragraph that answers all three feels complete, logical and convincing.","sz":9.3,"b":true},{"t":"h","x":"Worked example – Idea 6.8 (tourism, social drawback)"},{"t":"p","x":"IDEA There are several reasons why residents dislike tourism, one of which is that mass tourism causes overcrowding. EXPLANATION Because thousands of visitors arrive in the same season, narrow streets, buses and restaurants become packed, and residents lose access to their own neighbourhoods. RESULT This often leads to anger towards visitors, thereby damaging the friendly image of the city. EXAMPLE For example, a shopkeeper in an old town who needs twenty minutes to cross a crowded square may stop welcoming tourists altogether.","sz":7.0,"b":true},{"t":"h","x":"Upgrade ladder"},{"t":"table","head":["Version","Level"],"rows":[["Social media is bad. People waste time.","Thin: a statement with no development."],["Social media is bad because people waste time.","Better: one reason, but still general."],["When people scroll for hours, they lose track of time, which leads to unfinished work. For example, a student may miss his homework deadline.","Band 7+: idea → explanation → result → example."]]},{"t":"p","x":"PARAGRAPH CHECKLIST (use after every body paragraph) n ☐ One clear main idea in the topic sentence. n ☐ An explanation with when / if / because / as / by / through. n ☐ A result that follows logically (no new idea). n ☐ A realistic example (no invented statistics) starting with a clear phrase. n ☐ Natural chunks (collocations), not memorised long sentences.","sz":8.6,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"O‘ZBEKCHA IZOH","l":["Har bir gʻoyadan keyin oʻzingizdan soʻrang: Nega? (izoh), Natijasi nima? (natija), Masalan? (misol). Uchala savolga","javob bergan abzats toʻliq va ishonarli boʻladi."]}]},{"pn":7,"title":"Grammar Toolkit","sub":"Intro: paraphrasing and the While-sentence","blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"A. Four ways to paraphrase the topic"},{"t":"table","head":["Technique","How","Example"],"rows":[["1. Synonyms","harmful → damaging, negative; people → individuals; important → essential","Fast food is harmful. → Junk food has a damaging effect."],["2. Word family","verb → noun, adjective → adverb","Technology makes life easier. → Technological advances simplify daily life."],["3. Change the structure","active ↔ passive; noun phrase ↔ clause","Many students study abroad. → Studying overseas is chosen by a growing number of students."],["4. Change the opening","It is believed that… / A growing number of… / There is a debate about…","Some people say… → It is widely argued that…"]]},{"t":"p","x":"Do not change key words that have no good synonym (social media, online learning, working from home). Paraphrase around them.","sz":8.2,"b":true},{"t":"h","x":"B. The While-sentence (two sides in one sentence)"},{"t":"box","h":"FORMULA","l":["While some people argue that [side A], others believe that [side B].","While some people argue that remote work saves money, others believe that it weakens","teamwork."]},{"t":"table","head":["Pattern","Form","Example"],"rows":[["While / Whereas","While [A clause], [B clause].","While some prefer cities, others prefer the countryside."],["Opinions are divided","Opinions are divided on whether + clause.","Opinions are divided on whether children should have phones."],["It is often argued","It is often argued that…, but others…","It is often argued that homework is useless, but others disagree."],["Some … others …","Some people think…, whereas others feel…","Some people think games waste time, whereas others feel they teach skills."]]},{"t":"h","x":"C. Verbs for opinions (vary them!)"},{"t":"p","x":"argue / claim / maintain that… · believe / feel / think that… · are convinced / are of the opinion that…","sz":8.2,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"COMMON MISTAKES","l":["✗ While some people think…, but others… → ✓ never use but after while.","✗ Nowadays, technology is very very good. → ✓ avoid weak, repeated adverbs; use precise","adjectives.","✗ This essay will discuss about… → ✓ discuss + noun (no “about”)."]},{"t":"box","h":"O‘ZBEKCHA IZOH","l":["While = \"...boʻlsa-da / ...bir paytda\". Gapning bir qismida bir fikr, ikkinchi qismida qarama-qarshi fikr beriladi.","While’dan keyin but ishlatilmaydi."]}]},{"pn":8,"title":"Grammar Toolkit","sub":"Topic sentences: There are…, one of which is…","blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"A. Body 1 – introduce the opposite side"},{"t":"box","h":"FORMULA","l":["There are several / a number of / many + plural noun, one of which is + noun phrase /","that-clause.","There are several reasons why critics dislike social media, one of which is that it damages users’","self-esteem."]},{"t":"table","head":["Pattern","Example"],"rows":[["one of which is + noun phrase","There are several drawbacks of online learning, one of which is the lack of face-to-face interaction."],["one of which is that + clause","There are many benefits of tourism, one of which is that it creates jobs."],["the most important / common of which is","There are several reasons why people avoid cities, the most common of which is pollution."],["One of the most + adj + plural noun + is","One of the most serious problems of fast food is obesity."],["A major / key + noun + is","A key advantage of working remotely is flexibility."]]},{"t":"p","x":"Agreement check: There are + plural. Say benefits of / drawbacks of / advantages of a thing, not for. Say reasons why a thing happens.","sz":8.2,"b":true},{"t":"h","x":"B. Body 2 – state your opinion"},{"t":"box","h":"FORMULA","l":["However, I believe / am convinced / would argue / tend to think / firmly believe that [my side]","because [Idea 1].","However, I am convinced that working from home is better, mainly because it saves employees","money."]},{"t":"table","head":["Starter","Use"],"rows":[["However, I strongly believe that…","most confident, good for clear opinions"],["However, from my perspective,…","natural for personal opinion"],["However, I would argue that…","polite, academic"],["However, I tend to think that…","careful, balanced"],["However, I am of the opinion that…","formal"]]},{"t":"h","x":"C. Useful adjectives for ideas"},{"t":"p","x":"positive: significant, major, key, undeniable, practical, long-lasting negative: serious, harmful, damaging, hidden, long-term, costly","sz":8.2,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"COMMON MISTAKES","l":["✗ There is several reasons… → ✓ There are several reasons…","✗ I am agree with… → ✓ I agree with / I am convinced that…","✗ One of the biggest problem is… → ✓ One of the biggest problems is…","✗ In my opinion, I think… → ✓ use only one: In my opinion, / I think"]}]},{"pn":9,"title":"Grammar Toolkit","sub":"Explanation: when / if / because / as / by / through","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The explanation sentence answers “Why?” or “How?”. Use these six connectors and vary them from paragraph to paragraph.","sz":9.3,"b":true},{"t":"table","head":["Connec","Pattern","Meaning","Example"],"rows":[]},{"t":"p","x":"tor when when + subject + verb something that When people compare themselves with when + V-ing regularly happens influencers, they feel inadequate. if if + present simple, …can / a possible situation If students study alone, they can easily get may / will distracted. because because + subject + verb reason (clause) Because rents are high, many families cannot because of + noun / V-ing buy a home. as As + subject + verb, main reason (known fact, As large companies are in cities, jobs are easy to clause formal) find. by by + V-ing the means / the By skipping the commute, staff save time and method money. through through + noun / V-ing process or experience Learners improve through daily practice.","sz":8.2,"b":true},{"t":"h","x":"One idea, six explanations"},{"t":"p","x":"when When young people see perfect lives online, they begin to feel inadequate. if If young people see perfect lives online every day, they may start to feel inadequate. because Because influencers show only their best moments, young people feel inadequate. as As influencers show only their best moments, young people feel inadequate. by By comparing themselves with influencers, young people begin to feel inadequate. through Through constant exposure to perfect images, young people begin to feel inadequate.","sz":7.0,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"RULES TO REMEMBER","l":["Use present simple for general truths; add can / may / tend to to sound careful and academic.","because + clause but because of + noun: because of high prices, because prices are high.","by + V-ing shows how something is done; when shows a time or condition.","as at the beginning of a sentence means reason, not time. Put a comma after the clause."]},{"t":"box","h":"O‘ZBEKCHA IZOH","l":["when = qachonki; if = agar; because = chunki; as = chunki / ...ligi sababli; by + V-ing = ...ish orqali; through =","...orqali, ...davomida. Eslab qoling: because of dan keyin gap emas, ot keladi."]}]},{"pn":10,"title":"Grammar Toolkit","sub":"Result and Example: finish the chain","blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"A. Result – “So what happens?”"},{"t":"table","head":["Structure","Example"],"rows":[["which leads to / results in / contributes to + noun or V-ing","The cost of living is high, which leads to financial stress."],["thereby + V-ing","Students stay up late, thereby damaging their health."],["causing / making + object + (to) verb / adjective","Deadlines are tight, causing workers to feel exhausted."],["so + clause","Rents are high, so many young people live with their parents."],["As a result, / Consequently, / Therefore, + clause","As a result, they put more money aside every month."],["This, in turn, can + verb","Players lose sleep. This, in turn, can reduce their concentration."],["so + adj + that / such a + noun + that","The queue was so long that customers left."]]},{"t":"p","x":"Hedging keeps results realistic: can, may, could, tend to, be likely to, often, in many cases. Avoid always, everyone, never.","sz":8.2,"b":true},{"t":"h","x":"B. Example – “Can you show me?”"},{"t":"box","h":"EXAMPLE FORMULA","l":["For example, a / an + typical person + who + situation + may / could + result.","For example, a teenager who sees her friends’ holiday photos every day may feel that her own","life is boring."]},{"t":"table","head":["Starter","Example"],"rows":[["For example, / For instance,","For instance, an employee who spends $15 a day on lunch could save a lot at home."],["Take … as an example.","Take Tashkent as an example: rents rise, so students share flats."],["A good example of this is… / A case in point is…","A case in point is a pupil who copies answers and learns nothing."],["Consider + a person / a situation","Consider a nurse who works fourteen hours a day."],["Imagine + a person who…","Imagine a driver who spends two hours in traffic every day."]]},{"t":"box","h":"EXAMPLE RULES","l":["Use a typical person or situation (a student, a driver, a nurse) – not a long story.","Do not invent statistics (“70% of teens…”). Use small, realistic numbers only if they are","natural.","Use may / could so the example sounds believable.","An example illustrates the result; it should not introduce a new idea."]}]},{"pn":11,"title":"Grammar Toolkit","sub":"Concession and Conclusion: although / even though","blocks":[{"t":"box","h":"CONCLUSION FORMULA","l":["In conclusion, although / even though [opposite side clause], I firmly believe that [my","opinion] because [main reason].","In conclusion, although remote work may weaken teamwork, I firmly believe that it is better for","most employees because it saves time and money."]},{"t":"table","head":["Linker","Pattern","Example"],"rows":[["although / though","Although + clause, main clause.","Although studying abroad is expensive, it improves career prospects."],["even though","stronger than although","Even though fast food is cheap, it damages health."],["while / whereas","contrast of two facts","While cities are noisy, they offer better jobs."],["despite / in spite of","+ noun or V-ing","Despite the high cost, many students study abroad."],["despite the fact that","+ clause","Despite the fact that games are addictive, they teach teamwork."],["however / nevertheless","separate sentence + comma","Cities are noisy. However, they offer better jobs."]]},{"t":"h","x":"Same meaning – four ways"},{"t":"p","x":"although Although big cities are crowded, they offer better jobs. even though Even though big cities are crowded, they offer better jobs. despite Despite being crowded, big cities offer better jobs. however Big cities are crowded. However, they offer better jobs.","sz":7.0,"b":true},{"t":"box","h":"COMMON MISTAKES","l":["✗ Although it is expensive, but it is worth it. → ✓ Although it is expensive, it is worth it.","✗ Despite of the cost… → ✓ Despite the cost… / In spite of the cost…","✗ Despite it is expensive… → ✓ Despite being expensive… / Despite the fact that it is","expensive…","✗ In conclusion, although…, however… → ✓ use only one linker per contrast."]},{"t":"h","x":"Conclusion starters (choose one)"},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, although… To sum up, even though… Overall, while… I firmly believe that… I am convinced that… I would therefore argue that…","sz":8.6,"b":false},{"t":"box","h":"O‘ZBEKCHA IZOH","l":["although / even though = \"...boʻlsa ham\". Gapning ikkinchi qismida but ishlatilmaydi. Xulosada avval","qarama-qarshi tomonni (although), keyin oʻz fikringizni yozing."]}]},{"pn":12,"title":"Plug-and-Play Template","sub":"A natural, simple structure for every topic","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Fill the brackets with your own ideas from the Idea Bank. Keep the grammar frame – change only the content. It is a matter of debate whether [topic, paraphrased]. While some people argue that [side A], others believe that [side B]. This essay will discuss both views and explain why INTRO I support [my side]. There are several reasons why [people support side A], one of which is [Idea 1]. When / If / Because / As / By / Through [explanation], which leads to / thereby + BODY 1 V-ing [result]. For example, a [typical person] who [situation] may [result]. However, I believe / am convinced that [my side] because [Idea 1]. When / If / Because / As / By / Through [explanation], As a result, / This enables… [result]. BODY 2 For instance, [example]. In conclusion, although [side A], I firmly believe that [my side] because [main reason]. CONCLUSION","sz":9.3,"b":false},{"t":"h","x":"Power-chunk pack – swap in alternatives"},{"t":"p","x":"Intro opener It is widely debated whether… · People disagree about whether… · Opinions are divided on whether… Body 1 opener There are a number of reasons why…, the most important of which is… · Critics often point out that… Explanation When · If · Because · As · By + V-ing · Through + noun Result which leads to · thereby + V-ing · As a result, · Consequently, · This, in turn, can… Example For example, · For instance, · Take… as an example · A case in point is… Body 2 opener However, I firmly believe that… · However, from my perspective,… · However, I would argue that… Conclusion In conclusion, although… · To sum up, even though… · Overall, while… TIMING (40 minutes) 5 min plan (2 ideas + connectors) • 30 min write • 5 min check: articles, verb agreement, although/but, spelling.","sz":8.6,"b":false}]}],"ex":[{"n":1,"title":"Paraphrase The Topic","ins":"Rewrite each Task 2 statement in your own words. Use the hints. Do not copy the original structure.","items":[{"q":"Social media has a negative impact on young people.","o":[],"h":"harmful effect · teenagers · social networking sites"},{"q":"More people are working from home nowadays.","o":[],"h":"remote work · increasingly common"},{"q":"Children spend too much time playing video games.","o":[],"h":"kids · excessive · computer games"},{"q":"Some people think university education should be free.","o":[],"h":"higher education · ought to · at no cost"},{"q":"Fast food is harmful to health.","o":[],"h":"junk food · damaging · well-being"},{"q":"Many young people choose to study abroad.","o":[],"h":"a large number of · students · pursue education overseas"},{"q":"Online shopping has replaced traditional shopping.","o":[],"h":"internet purchasing · taking the place of · physical stores"},{"q":"Technology makes our lives easier.","o":[],"h":"modern devices · simplify · daily life"}]},{"n":2,"title":"While-Sentences","ins":"Join Side A and Side B into one sentence beginning with While. Add believe / argue / think / feel.","items":[{"q":"A: Some people say online learning is more convenient. B: Others say classroom learning is more effective.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A: Some people think working from home saves money. B: Others think it harms teamwork.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A: Some people believe that children should have a phone. B: Others believe phones are dangerous for young kids.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A: Some people prefer living in big cities. B: Others prefer small towns.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A: Some people think video games waste time. B: Others think they develop useful skills.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A: Some people think everyone should volunteer. B: Others think it should be a personal choice.","o":[],"h":""}]},{"n":3,"title":"There Are…, One Of Which Is…","ins":"Choose the correct word or phrase to complete each Body 1 topic sentence.","items":[{"q":"There are several drawbacks of social media, one of ____ is its effect on sleep.","o":["that","which","them","what"],"h":""},{"q":"There are a number of ____ why people choose to work remotely.","o":["reasoned","reasoning","reason","reasons"],"h":""},{"q":"There ____ many benefits of volunteering, one of which is improved confidence.","o":["are","has","have","is"],"h":""},{"q":"One of the most serious ____ of fast food is obesity.","o":["problematic","problematically","problems","problem"],"h":""},{"q":"There are two main advantages of studying abroad, the first of ____ is better job prospects.","o":["which","what","that","it"],"h":""},{"q":"There are several reasons ____ some parents dislike homework, the most common of which is stress.","o":["whose","what","why","when"],"h":""},{"q":"There are several advantages ____ working from home.","o":["by","of","at","from"],"h":""},{"q":"There are many benefits of tourism, ____ of which is job creation.","o":["a","ones","that","one"],"h":""}]},{"n":4,"title":"Explanation Connectors","ins":"Choose the best connector. Think about the grammar that must follow it.","items":[{"q":"____ people sit at a screen all day, they often suffer from back pain.","o":["Through","Because of","When","By"],"h":""},{"q":"Employees can save money ____ skipping the daily commute.","o":["by","as","so","because"],"h":""},{"q":"Young people learn to manage money ____ part-time jobs.","o":["if","because","as","through"],"h":""},{"q":"Children may fall behind at school ____ they spend too long on their phones.","o":["because of","if","by","through"],"h":""},{"q":"____ prices in tourist areas have risen sharply, many locals can no longer afford to live there.","o":["By","Through","Because of","As"],"h":""},{"q":"Workers feel exhausted ____ their long working hours.","o":["because of","if","as","because"],"h":""},{"q":"Gamers can earn a living ____ streaming their games.","o":["because","so","by","as"],"h":""},{"q":"Online shoppers often spend more than planned ____ flash sales create a sense of urgency.","o":["because of","because","by","through"],"h":""},{"q":"Volunteers feel proud ____ they see their efforts change someone’s life.","o":["when","because of","by","through"],"h":""},{"q":"Workers burn out quickly ____ they never switch off.","o":["through","by","if","because of"],"h":""}]},{"n":5,"title":"Add The Result","ins":"Combine the two sentences with the structure in brackets. You may change small words.","items":[{"q":"People compare themselves with influencers. They lose self-esteem. [which leads to]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Students stay up late studying. They suffer from sleep deprivation. [thereby + V-ing]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Rents in cities are very high. Many families cannot afford a home. [As a result,]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Fast food contains a lot of fat. People gain weight. [which results in]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Workers have too many deadlines. They feel stressed. [causing + object + to]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Players spend hours gaming. They neglect their studies. [This, in turn, …]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Tourists crowd the old town. Residents feel annoyed. [so many … that]","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Online courses are cheap. More people can study. [, enabling + object + to]","o":[],"h":""}]},{"n":6,"title":"Build The Example","ins":"Turn the notes into one natural example sentence. Start with the phrase given.","items":[{"q":"For example, teenager · sees friends’ holiday photos · feels her life is boring","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"For instance, employee · spends $15 a day on bus and lunch · saves $300 a month at home","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Take … as an example. Tashkent · rents rise · young people share flats","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A good example of this is a student · plays games until midnight · cannot wake up for class","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"A case in point is a pupil · copies answers · learns nothing","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Consider a nurse · works 14 hours · makes mistakes","o":[],"h":""}]},{"n":7,"title":"However, I…","ins":"Choose the most natural and correct topic sentence for Body 2. Three options contain grammar mistakes.","items":[{"q":"Topic: online learning is better A However, in my opinion is online learning the better option. B However, I believe that online learning is the better option for most students. C However, I am agree that online learning is the better option. D However, I think online learning good for students.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Topic: fast food A However, my opinion say that fast food drawbacks are bigger. B However, I am convince that the drawbacks of fast food outweigh its benefits. C However, I am thinking fast food is very bad. D However, I am convinced that the drawbacks of fast food outweigh its benefits.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Topic: volunteering A However, I would argue that volunteering is worthwhile because it builds confidence. B However, I would argue volunteering worthwhile because of it builds confidence. C However, I argue that volunteering are worthwhile because it build confidence. D However, I would argues that volunteering is worthwhile.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Topic: long working hours A However, from my perspective is working long hours not worth it. B However, from my perspective, working long hours not worth damage to health. C However, for my perspective, working long hours is not worth it. D However, from my perspective, working long hours is not worth the damage to one’s health.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Topic: cashless payments A However, I tend to think that cashless payments is more convenient. B However, I tend think that cashless payments more convenient. C However, I tend to think that cashless payments are more convenient. D However, I tending to think cashless payments are convenient.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Topic: public transport A However, I firmly believe that governments should to invest in public transport. B However, I firmly believe that governments should invest in public transport. C However, I firmly believing governments should invest in public transport. D However, firmly I believe that governments should invested in public transport.","o":[],"h":""}]},{"n":8,"title":"Sort The Paragraph","ins":"Each paragraph has four jumbled sentences. Write the correct order of letters (Idea → Explanation → Result → Example), then label each sentence.","items":[{"q":"Paragraph A · Video games (drawback)","sents":["For example, a student who plays until midnight may fail to hand in his homework the next morning.","There are several risks of gaming, one of which is that players may neglect their studies.","As a result, their grades decline, which upsets teachers and parents alike.","When games become more exciting than school, players lose track of time and put their homework off."]},{"q":"Paragraph B · Working from home (benefit)","sents":["This allows them to spend more time with their families and to sleep longer.","However, I believe working from home is better because it removes the daily commute.","For instance, someone who travels two hours a day can gain over ten hours of free time each week.","By skipping crowded buses and traffic jams, employees save both time and energy."]},{"q":"Paragraph C · Online shopping (drawback)","sents":["Consequently, they often spend money on things they do not need.","There are several reasons why online shopping can damage budgets, one of which is impulse buying.","For example, someone who only wanted a phone case may end up ordering three extra gadgets at a discount.","Because flash sales and targeted ads appear on every screen, shoppers feel pressured to buy immediately."]}]},{"n":9,"title":"Error Correction","ins":"Each sentence contains one grammar mistake from this book. Find it and write the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"Social media makes people feels lonely.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"There is several reasons why teenagers use phones.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Although it is expensive, but studying abroad is worth it.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"By work from home, employees save money.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"One of the biggest problem is traffic.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Because of students stay up late, they feel tired.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Working long hours lead to stress and burnout.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"For example, a student who study abroad may feel homesick.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Despite of the high cost, many people travel abroad.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Online shopping causes people spending more money.","o":[],"h":""}]},{"n":10,"title":"In Conclusion, Although…","ins":" 10 Write one conclusion sentence for each pair. Begin with In conclusion, although / even though and add your opinion.","items":[{"q":"Opposite side: Remote work may weaken teamwork. My opinion: It saves time and money.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Opposite side: Video games can be addictive. My opinion: They develop useful skills when played in moderation.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Opposite side: Studying abroad is expensive. My opinion: It improves career prospects.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Opposite side: Fast food is cheap and convenient. My opinion: It damages health in the long run.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Opposite side: Big cities are noisy and crowded. My opinion: They offer better jobs.","o":[],"h":""},{"q":"Opposite side: Homework causes stress. My opinion: It helps students build self-discipline.","o":[],"h":""}]},{"n":11,"title":"Idea Lab","ins":"Write a full chain (Idea → Explanation → Result → Example) for each idea using the suggested starters. About 60–80 words.","items":[{"q":"Air pollution increases the risk of respiratory problems.","h":"Explanation: because | Result: which leads to | Example: For example,","c":"7.6","o":[]},{"q":"Remote workers can save a considerable amount of money.","h":"Explanation: by + V-ing | Result: As a result, | Example: For instance,","c":"2.9","o":[]},{"q":"Players may lose track of time and neglect their studies.","h":"Explanation: when | Result: thereby + V-ing | Example: Take … as an example.","c":"8.4","o":[]},{"q":"Without supervision, students get easily distracted.","h":"Explanation: if | Result: This, in turn, … | Example: A good example of this is","c":"3.4","o":[]},{"q":"Volunteer experience strengthens a CV.","h":"Explanation: because | Result: which results in | Example: For example,","c":"20.9","o":[]},{"q":"Excessive screen time contributes to childhood obesity.","h":"Explanation: as | Result: causing + object + to | Example: For instance,","c":"4.6","o":[]}]},{"n":12,"title":"Task 2 Planning","ins":"Plan a full Task 2 essay for each prompt: paraphrase + While-sentence, Body 1 chain, Body 2 chain, conclusion. Borrow ideas from the Idea Bank using the codes.","items":[{"q":"Some people believe social media does more harm than good. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 1.2 · 1.4 · 1.6 · Body 2: 1.1 · 1.3 · 1.7"},{"q":"Online courses are replacing classroom learning. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 3.2 · 3.8 · 3.10 · Body 2: 3.3 · 3.9 · 3.7"},{"q":"More and more students study abroad. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages.","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 5.2 · 5.8 · 5.10 · Body 2: 5.1 · 5.7 · 5.9"},{"q":"Some people prefer big cities, others prefer small towns. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 7.2 · 7.6 · 7.10 · Body 2: 7.1 · 7.9 · 7.7"},{"q":"Fast food has become part of modern life. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 11.1 · 11.9 · 11.7 · Body 2: 11.6 · 11.8 · 11.10"},{"q":"Learning a foreign language is more important than ever. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 13.2 · 13.8 · 13.10 · Body 2: 13.3 · 13.7 · 13.9"},{"q":"Some young people take a year off before university. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 15.1 · 15.3 · 15.9 · Body 2: 15.2 · 15.4 · 15.10"},{"q":"More young adults are living with their parents. Is this a positive or negative development?","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 17.1 · 17.7 · 17.9 · Body 2: 17.2 · 17.4 · 17.10"},{"q":"Some people choose well-paid jobs with long working hours. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 19.7 · 19.9 · 19.3 · Body 2: 19.2 · 19.6 · 19.8"},{"q":"Some people think everyone should do volunteer work. Discuss both views","o":[],"h":"Body 1: 20.2 · 20.4 · 20.10"},{"q":"and give your opinion.","o":[],"h":"Body 2: 20.1 · 20.3 · 20.9"}]}],"essays":[{"pn":63,"title":"Social Media","q":"Some people believe that social media has had a negative effect on people’s lives, while others think it has improved them. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","paras":["People disagree about whether social networking sites have damaged or enriched modern life. While some argue that these platforms harm their users, others believe that they make everyday life easier and more enjoyable. This essay will discuss both views, although I personally believe that the advantages are greater, especially for people’s emotional well-being.","There are several reasons why critics dislike social media, one of which is that it «damages users’ self-esteem». When young people constantly compare themselves with the polished lives of influencers, they begin to «feel inadequate» about their own appearance and achievements. This often leads to anxiety and low mood, thereby making them even more desperate for online approval. In the long term, this constant pressure can even push young people to spend more time online, which only makes the problem worse. For example, a teenage girl who sees her classmates posting luxury holidays every week may become convinced that her own life is boring.","However, I believe that social media improves our lives because it helps people «feel less lonely». By «staying in touch» with family and friends through messages and video calls, users can share daily news and receive support, even when thousands of kilometres separate them. As a result, they feel valued and connected, which greatly improves their emotional well-being. This support is especially valuable for people who live far from home, because it gives them a daily sense of belonging. For instance, a student living abroad can speak to his parents every evening, so homesickness becomes much easier to handle.","In conclusion, although social media may harm the confidence of some users, I firmly believe that it improves modern life because it keeps families and friends close, whatever the distance, and I therefore think its benefits outweigh its risks."],"xray":{"head":["Paragraph","Idea","Explanation","Result","Example"],"rows":[["Body 1 · opposite side","1.2 (emotional ▼)","When","thereby + V-ing","For example,"],["Body 2 · my opinion","1.1 (emotional ▲)","By + V-ing","As a result, … which + verb","For instance,"]]}},{"pn":64,"title":"Working from Home","q":"Some people think that working from home is better for employees, while others believe that working in an office is better. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","paras":["Whether staff should work in a company office or from their own homes is a widely debated issue. While some people believe that the office is the best place to work, others prefer the flexibility of remote work. This essay will discuss both views before explaining why I support working from home.","There are several reasons why some employers insist on office work, one of which is that teamwork may suffer when people work remotely. When colleagues are in different places, «spontaneous conversations» disappear, and «misunderstandings occur» more often because instructions are written rather than explained. This can slow down projects, thereby frustrating both managers and customers. In addition, new employees may feel unsure about their duties, because nobody is sitting nearby to guide them through the first weeks. For example, a designer who cannot quickly ask a developer a question may wait hours for an email reply, which delays the whole product launch.","However, I believe that working from home is better, mainly because it helps employees «save a considerable amount of money». By skipping the daily journey to work, staff no longer pay «transport and fuel costs», and they can prepare cheap meals at home instead of buying expensive lunches. As a result, they can put more money aside every month, which reduces financial stress. This money can then be spent on savings, hobbies or family needs, so remote work improves their overall quality of life. For instance, an employee who spends fifteen dollars a day on bus tickets and lunch could keep more than three hundred dollars a month by staying at home.","In conclusion, although remote work may weaken teamwork, I firmly believe that it is the better option for most employees, as it saves them money, time and energy, and I therefore think companies should offer this choice."],"xray":{"head":["Paragraph","Idea","Explanation","Result","Example"],"rows":[["Body 1 · opposite side","2.8 (social ▼)","When","thereby + V-ing","For example,"],["Body 2 · my opinion","2.9 (financial ▲)","By + V-ing","As a result, … which + verb","For instance,"]]}},{"pn":65,"title":"Studying Abroad","q":"Some people believe that students should study abroad, while others think it is better to study in their own country. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","paras":["People hold different views about whether young people should pursue their education overseas or at home. While some believe that staying in one’s own country is the wiser choice, others argue that studying abroad offers more valuable experience. This essay will discuss both sides and explain why I support the latter.","There are a number of risks of studying abroad, one of which is that many international students «suffer from homesickness». Because they are far from familiar food, language and family, they often «find it hard to adapt» to a new culture, particularly during the first months. This can reduce their concentration and results, thereby making the experience less rewarding than expected. In addition, the high cost of living abroad adds to their worries, so some students return home before finishing their degrees. For example, a first-year student who phones his mother in tears every night may skip lectures and fall behind his classmates.","However, I believe that studying abroad is the better option because it «boosts students’ self-confidence». When young people have to rent a flat, deal with paperwork and make friends alone, they learn that they can solve problems without their parents’ help. Consequently, they become more resilient and independent, which prepares them well for adult life. These qualities are highly valued by employers, so graduates with international experience often find better positions. For instance, a graduate who has lived abroad for four years is usually far more comfortable giving presentations or travelling for work than one who has never left home.","In conclusion, although studying abroad can cause homesickness at first, I firmly believe that it is more beneficial, since it builds the confidence and independence that young people need in their careers, and I therefore think families should support this decision."],"xray":{"head":["Paragraph","Idea","Explanation","Result","Example"],"rows":[["Body 1 · opposite side","5.2 (emotional ▼)","Because","thereby + V-ing","For example,"],["Body 2 · my opinion","5.1 (emotional ▲)","When","Consequently, … which + verb","For instance,"]]}},{"pn":66,"title":"Living in Big Cities","q":"Some people prefer to live in big cities, while others prefer small towns. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","paras":["It is a matter of debate whether big cities or small towns are better places to live. While some people are attracted by the excitement of urban life, others prefer the peace of smaller communities. In my opinion, big cities offer more advantages, and I will explain why in this essay.","There are several reasons why people avoid large cities, one of which is that pollution «increases the risk of» health problems. Because millions of vehicles and factories release harmful gases every day, residents breathe dirty air, especially when traffic is heavy, and this can cause «respiratory problems». Over time, it may lead to chronic illnesses such as asthma, thereby increasing the number of hospital visits. As a result, families may spend a large part of their income on medicine, which creates additional stress for parents. For example, children who grow up beside busy highways are more likely to cough constantly and miss school.","However, I prefer big cities because they provide «a wide range of job opportunities». As large companies, banks and start-ups are concentrated in urban areas, graduates can easily find positions that match their skills, and they often receive «higher salaries». This enables them to build successful careers and gain financial stability much earlier. In addition, higher earnings allow young people to rent better homes and save for the future, which small towns rarely make possible. For instance, a software engineer in a capital city can compare dozens of offers, while someone in a remote village may have no choice at all.","In conclusion, although pollution is a serious problem in big cities, I firmly believe that urban life is preferable because it offers better jobs, higher incomes and brighter prospects for young people, and I therefore think young people should consider moving there."],"xray":{"head":["Paragraph","Idea","Explanation","Result","Example"],"rows":[["Body 1 · opposite side","7.6 (physical ▼)","Because … especially when","Over time, … thereby + V-ing","For example,"],["Body 2 · my opinion","7.9 (financial ▲)","As","This enables them to + verb","For instance,"]]}},{"pn":67,"title":"Smartphones for Children","q":"Many parents now give smartphones to young children. Do the advantages of this outweigh the disadvantages?","paras":["Nowadays, it is increasingly common for parents to buy mobile phones for their young children. While this practice has some clear benefits, it also creates serious problems for children’s development. In my opinion, the drawbacks are more significant than the advantages, especially for young children’s education.","There are several advantages of giving children phones, one of which is that it gives them «a sense of security». Because parents can «reach» their child at any moment, they can quickly check whether he has arrived safely at school or needs help, and the child knows that support is always one call away. This reduces anxiety for both sides, thereby allowing families to live more calmly. In addition, parents feel calmer at work, because they know that their child can contact them whenever necessary. For example, a ten-year-old who gets lost on the way home can call his mother immediately instead of panicking in the street.","However, I believe the disadvantages are greater, mainly because heavy phone use «hinders concentration». When children check notifications, watch short videos and play games all evening, they find it difficult to focus on one task, and their homework is often left unfinished. As a result, their marks decline and they «fall behind at school», which can damage their future opportunities. Moreover, the habit of constant entertainment makes ordinary lessons seem boring, so children lose interest in studying altogether. For instance, a pupil who spends four hours a day on his phone may struggle to understand a chapter that his classmates finish in twenty minutes.","In conclusion, although phones can make children feel safer, I firmly believe that their negative effect on learning is more serious, so parents should limit screen time for young children, and I therefore think strict time limits are essential."],"xray":{"head":["Paragraph","Idea","Explanation","Result","Example"],"rows":[["Body 1 · opposite side","4.1 (emotional ▲)","Because","thereby + V-ing","For example,"],["Body 2 · my opinion","4.4 (mental ▼)","When","As a result, … which + verb","For instance,"]]}}],"bank":[{"n":1,"title":"Social Media","uz":"Ijtimoiy tarmoqlar","q":"Some people believe social media does more harm than good to individuals. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"1.1","p":true,"en":"Social media helps people feel less lonely, as they can stay in touch with loved ones every day.","uz":"Ijtimoiy tarmoqlar odamlarning oʻzini yolgʻiz his qilishini kamaytiradi, chunki ular yaqinlari bilan har kuni aloqada boʻla oladi.","ch":[["feel less lonely","oʻzini kamroq yolgʻiz his qilmoq"],["stay in touch","aloqada boʻlib turmoq"]]},{"c":"1.2","p":false,"en":"Constantly comparing themselves with others can damage users’ self-esteem and make them feel inadequate.","uz":"Oʻzini doim boshqalar bilan solishtirish foydalanuvchilarning oʻziga boʻlgan hurmatiga putur yetkazadi va ularni oʻzini yetarli emasdek his qilishga olib keladi.","ch":[["damage self-esteem","oʻzini hurmat qilishga putur yetkazmoq"],["feel inadequate","oʻzini yetarli emasdek his qilmoq"]]},{"c":"1.3","p":true,"en":"Online platforms let people broaden their horizons and pick up new skills through free video tutorials.","uz":"Onlayn platformalar odamlarga dunyoqarashini kengaytirish va bepul video darslar orqali yangi koʻnikmalarni oʻrganib olish imkonini beradi.","ch":[["broaden one’s horizons","dunyoqarashni kengaytirmoq"],["pick up new skills","yangi koʻnikmalarni oʻrganib olmoq"]]},{"c":"1.4","p":false,"en":"Endless scrolling makes it hard to concentrate on important tasks and shortens people’s attention span.","uz":"Cheksiz skroll qilish muhim ishlarga e’tiborni qaratishni qiyinlashtiradi va odamlarning diqqat davomiyligini qisqartiradi.","ch":[["hard to concentrate","diqqatni jamlash qiyin"],["shorten attention span","diqqat davomiyligini qisqartirmoq"]]},{"c":"1.5","p":true,"en":"Online fitness communities motivate people to exercise by sharing free workout routines.","uz":"Onlayn sport jamoalari bepul mashq dasturlarini ulashib, odamlarni sport bilan shugʻullanishga undaydi.","ch":[["motivate people to exercise","odamlarni sport qilishga undamoq"],["workout routine","mashqlar dasturi"]]},{"c":"1.6","p":false,"en":"Spending hours on screens often leads to a sedentary lifestyle and disrupted sleep patterns.","uz":"Soatlab ekran qarshisida oʻtirish koʻpincha kam harakatli turmush tarziga va uyqu tartibining buzilishiga olib keladi.","ch":[["sedentary lifestyle","kam harakatli turmush tarzi"],["disrupted sleep patterns","buzilgan uyqu tartibi"]]},{"c":"1.7","p":true,"en":"Users can build a wide network of friends and share common interests regardless of distance.","uz":"Foydalanuvchilar masofadan qat’i nazar, keng doʻstlar doirasini shakllantirib, umumiy qiziqishlarini boʻlisha oladi.","ch":[["build a wide network","keng aloqalar doirasini yaratmoq"],["share common interests","umumiy qiziqishlarni boʻlishmoq"]]},{"c":"1.8","p":false,"en":"Face-to-face interaction gradually declines, so people may drift apart from relatives living under the same roof.","uz":"Yuzma-yuz muloqot asta-sekin kamayadi, shuning uchun odamlar bir uyda yashaydigan qarindoshlaridan ham uzoqlashib qolishi mumkin.","ch":[["face-to-face interaction","yuzma-yuz muloqot"],["drift apart","bir-biridan uzoqlashib qolmoq"]]},{"c":"1.9","p":true,"en":"Small businesses can reach a global audience at minimal advertising costs.","uz":"Kichik bizneslar reklamaga juda oz mablagʻ sarflab, butun dunyo auditoriyasiga chiqa oladi.","ch":[["reach a global audience","global auditoriyaga yetib bormoq"],["minimal advertising costs","minimal reklama xarajatlari"]]},{"c":"1.10","p":false,"en":"Targeted ads encourage impulse buying, so users often overspend on things they do not need.","uz":"Maqsadli reklamalar oʻylamasdan xarid qilishga undaydi, shuning uchun foydalanuvchilar koʻpincha keraksiz narsalarga ortiqcha pul sarflaydi.","ch":[["impulse buying","oʻylamasdan xarid qilish"],["overspend","ortiqcha pul sarflamoq"]]}]},{"n":2,"title":"Working from Home","uz":"Uydan turib ishlash","q":"Some people think working from home is better than working in an office. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"2.1","p":true,"en":"Employees feel more in control when they can set their own schedule.","uz":"Xodimlar oʻz ish jadvalini oʻzlari belgilay olsa, vaziyatni koʻproq nazorat qilayotganini his qiladi.","ch":[["feel in control","vaziyatni nazorat qilayotgandek his qilmoq"],["set one’s own schedule","oʻz jadvalini oʻzi belgilamoq"]]},{"c":"2.2","p":false,"en":"Working alone for long periods can make people feel isolated and cut off from their colleagues.","uz":"Uzoq vaqt yolgʻiz ishlash odamlarni oʻzini ajralib qolgandek his qilishga va hamkasblaridan uzilib qolishga olib kelishi mumkin.","ch":[["feel isolated","oʻzini ajralib qolgandek his qilmoq"],["cut off from","...dan uzilib qolmoq"]]},{"c":"2.3","p":true,"en":"Without office noise and interruptions, people can stay focused and get more done in less time.","uz":"Ofisdagi shovqin va xalaqitlarsiz odamlar diqqatini jamlab, kamroq vaqtda koʻproq ish bitira oladi.","ch":[["stay focused","diqqatni jamlab turmoq"],["get more done","koʻproq ish bitirmoq"]]},{"c":"2.4","p":false,"en":"When work and home life blur together, employees struggle to switch off and soon burn out.","uz":"Ish va shaxsiy hayot aralashib ketsa, xodimlar ishdan uzilib dam ola olmaydi va tez orada ruhan holdan toyadi.","ch":[["blur together","aralashib ketmoq"],["switch off","ish haqida oʻylashni toʻxtatib dam olmoq"],["burn out","ruhan holdan toymoq"]]},{"c":"2.5","p":true,"en":"Skipping the commute cuts down on stress and leaves more time to get enough sleep.","uz":"Har kungi yoʻlga sarflanadigan vaqtdan qutulish stressni kamaytiradi va yetarlicha uxlash uchun koʻproq vaqt qoldiradi.","ch":[["skip the commute","ishga qatnashdan qutulmoq"],["get enough sleep","yetarlicha uxlamoq"]]},{"c":"2.6","p":false,"en":"Sitting at a laptop all day often causes back and neck pain, especially without proper office furniture.","uz":"Kun boʻyi noutbuk oldida oʻtirish, ayniqsa maxsus ofis mebeli boʻlmasa, koʻpincha bel va boʻyin ogʻrigʻiga sabab boʻladi.","ch":[["back and neck pain","bel va boʻyin ogʻrigʻi"],["proper office furniture","toʻgʻri ofis jihozlari"]]},{"c":"2.7","p":true,"en":"Remote workers can spend more quality time with their families and be there for important moments.","uz":"Uydan ishlaydiganlar oilasi bilan koʻproq sifatli vaqt oʻtkaza oladi va muhim onlarda yonida boʻla oladi.","ch":[["spend quality time","sifatli vaqt oʻtkazmoq"],["be there for","...da yonida boʻlmoq"]]},{"c":"2.8","p":false,"en":"Teamwork may suffer because spontaneous conversations disappear and misunderstandings occur more often.","uz":"Jamoaviy ish yomonlashishi mumkin, chunki beixtiyor suhbatlar yoʻqoladi va tushunmovchiliklar tez-tez yuz beradi.","ch":[["spontaneous conversations","rejalashtirilmagan suhbatlar"],["misunderstandings occur","tushunmovchilik yuzaga kelmoq"]]},{"c":"2.9","p":true,"en":"Employees can save a considerable amount of money on transport and fuel costs.","uz":"Xodimlar transport va yoqilgʻi xarajatlarida ancha pul tejashi mumkin.","ch":[["save a considerable amount of money","anchagina pul tejamoq"],["transport and fuel costs","transport va yoqilgʻi xarajatlari"]]},{"c":"2.10","p":false,"en":"Staff must cover extra costs such as electricity and internet, and remote workers are sometimes overlooked for promotion.","uz":"Xodimlar elektr va internet kabi qoʻshimcha xarajatlarni oʻzi qoplashi kerak, uydan ishlaydiganlar esa ba’zan lavozim koʻtarilishida e’tibordan chetda qoladi.","ch":[["cover extra costs","qoʻshimcha xarajatlarni qoplamoq"],["overlooked for promotion","lavozim koʻtarilishida e’tibordan chetda qolmoq"]]}]},{"n":3,"title":"Online Learning","uz":"Onlayn ta’lim","q":"Some people say online courses are better than classroom learning. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"3.1","p":true,"en":"Shy students feel more confident asking questions from behind a screen.","uz":"Uyatchan oʻquvchilar ekran ortidan savol berishda oʻzini ancha ishonchli his qiladi.","ch":[["feel more confident","oʻzini ishonchliroq his qilmoq"],["from behind a screen","ekran ortidan"]]},{"c":"3.2","p":false,"en":"Studying alone can make students lose motivation and feel disconnected from their classmates.","uz":"Yolgʻiz oʻqish talabalarning motivatsiyasini yoʻqotishi va sinfdoshlaridan uzilib qolgandek his qilishiga sabab boʻlishi mumkin.","ch":[["lose motivation","motivatsiyani yoʻqotmoq"],["feel disconnected","aloqani yoʻqotgandek his qilmoq"]]},{"c":"3.3","p":true,"en":"Learners can study at their own pace and replay lessons until they fully understand.","uz":"Oʻquvchilar oʻz sur’atida oʻqib, mavzuni toʻliq tushunmaguncha darslarni qayta koʻrishi mumkin.","ch":[["study at one’s own pace","oʻz sur’atida oʻqimoq"],["replay lessons","darslarni qayta koʻrmoq"]]},{"c":"3.4","p":false,"en":"Without a teacher’s supervision, many students get easily distracted and put off their assignments.","uz":"Oʻqituvchi nazoratisiz koʻp talabalar osongina chalgʻib, topshiriqlarini keyinga suradi.","ch":[["get easily distracted","osongina chalgʻib qolmoq"],["put off","keyinga surmoq"]]},{"c":"3.5","p":true,"en":"Students avoid tiring journeys to school, so they have more energy for studying.","uz":"Oʻquvchilar maktabga charchatuvchi yoʻldan qutuladi, shuning uchun oʻqishga koʻproq kuch-quvvati qoladi.","ch":[["tiring journey","charchatuvchi yoʻl"],["have more energy","koʻproq kuch-quvvatga ega boʻlmoq"]]},{"c":"3.6","p":false,"en":"Long hours in front of a screen can cause eye strain and frequent headaches.","uz":"Ekran qarshisida uzoq oʻtirish koʻzning charchashi va tez-tez bosh ogʻrishiga sabab boʻlishi mumkin.","ch":[["eye strain","koʻzning charchashi"],["frequent headaches","tez-tez boʻladigan bosh ogʻrigʻi"]]},{"c":"3.7","p":true,"en":"Learners can connect with peers from other countries and learn from experts around the world.","uz":"Oʻquvchilar boshqa mamlakatlardagi tengdoshlari bilan aloqa oʻrnatib, dunyo boʻylab mutaxassislardan oʻrganishi mumkin.","ch":[["connect with peers","tengdoshlar bilan aloqa oʻrnatmoq"],["learn from experts","mutaxassislardan oʻrganmoq"]]},{"c":"3.8","p":false,"en":"Students miss out on classroom interaction, so they may struggle to develop teamwork skills.","uz":"Talabalar sinfdagi muloqotdan mahrum boʻladi, shuning uchun jamoada ishlash koʻnikmalarini rivojlantirishda qiynalishi mumkin.","ch":[["miss out on","...dan mahrum boʻlmoq"],["struggle to develop teamwork skills","jamoada ishlash koʻnikmalarini rivojlantirishda qiynalmoq"]]},{"c":"3.9","p":true,"en":"Online courses are far more affordable, as students save on accommodation and transport.","uz":"Onlayn kurslar ancha arzon, chunki talabalar yashash joyi va transportga pul sarflamaydi.","ch":[["far more affordable","ancha hamyonbop"],["save on accommodation","turar joy xarajatlarini tejamoq"]]},{"c":"3.10","p":false,"en":"Reliable devices and fast internet are a heavy financial burden for low-income families.","uz":"Ishonchli qurilmalar va tezkor internet kam daromadli oilalar uchun ogʻir moliyaviy yuk boʻladi.","ch":[["a financial burden","moliyaviy yuk"],["low-income families","kam daromadli oilalar"]]}]},{"n":4,"title":"Smartphones for Children","uz":"Bolalarga smartfon berish","q":"Many parents give smartphones to young children. Do the advantages of this outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"4.1","p":true,"en":"A phone gives children a sense of security, as they can reach their parents at any time.","uz":"Telefon bolalarga xavfsizlik hissini beradi, chunki ular istalgan vaqtda ota-onasi bilan bogʻlana oladi.","ch":[["a sense of security","xavfsizlik hissi"],["reach one’s parents","ota-onasi bilan bogʻlanmoq"]]},{"c":"4.2","p":false,"en":"Children glued to screens often become irritable and throw tantrums when their phones are taken away.","uz":"Telefonga yopishib olgan bolalar telefoni olib qoʻyilganda koʻpincha serjahl boʻlib, injiqlik qiladi.","ch":[["glued to screens","ekranga yopishib qolgan"],["throw a tantrum","injiqlik qilmoq"]]},{"c":"4.3","p":true,"en":"Educational apps help kids learn through play and improve their problem-solving skills.","uz":"Ta’limiy ilovalar bolalarga oʻynab oʻrganishga va masalalarni yechish koʻnikmasini yaxshilashga yordam beradi.","ch":[["learn through play","oʻyin orqali oʻrganmoq"],["problem-solving skills","muammolarni hal qilish koʻnikmalari"]]},{"c":"4.4","p":false,"en":"Heavy phone use hinders concentration, so children fall behind at school.","uz":"Telefondan haddan ziyod foydalanish diqqatni jamlashga xalaqit beradi, natijada bolalar maktabda ortda qolib ketadi.","ch":[["hinder concentration","diqqatni jamlashga xalaqit bermoq"],["fall behind","ortda qolmoq"]]},{"c":"4.5","p":true,"en":"Some apps track daily steps and encourage children to stay active through fun challenges.","uz":"Ba’zi ilovalar kundalik qadamlarni hisoblab, qiziqarli musobaqalar orqali bolalarni harakatchan boʻlishga undaydi.","ch":[["track daily steps","kundalik qadamlarni kuzatmoq"],["stay active","harakatchan boʻlib turmoq"]]},{"c":"4.6","p":false,"en":"Excessive screen time contributes to childhood obesity and poor posture.","uz":"Ekran oldida haddan tashqari koʻp vaqt oʻtkazish bolalardagi semirish va notoʻgʻri qad-qomatga sabab boʻladi.","ch":[["childhood obesity","bolalardagi semizlik"],["poor posture","notoʻgʻri qad-qomat"]]},{"c":"4.7","p":true,"en":"Video calls let children keep in touch with relatives abroad and make friends who share their hobbies.","uz":"Video qoʻngʻiroqlar bolalarga chet eldagi qarindoshlari bilan aloqada boʻlish va qiziqishlari oʻxshash doʻstlar orttirish imkonini beradi.","ch":[["keep in touch with relatives","qarindoshlar bilan aloqada boʻlmoq"],["make friends","doʻst orttirmoq"]]},{"c":"4.8","p":false,"en":"Kids may neglect real-life friendships and become targets of cyberbullying.","uz":"Bolalar real hayotdagi doʻstliklarni e’tiborsiz qoldirishi va kiberbulling nishoniga aylanishi mumkin.","ch":[["neglect friendships","doʻstliklarni e’tiborsiz qoldirmoq"],["target of cyberbullying","kiberbulling nishoni"]]},{"c":"4.9","p":true,"en":"Child-friendly banking apps teach kids to manage their pocket money and develop saving habits.","uz":"Bolalar uchun moʻljallangan bank ilovalari ularga choʻntak pulini boshqarishni va tejamkorlik odatini shakllantirishni oʻrgatadi.","ch":[["manage pocket money","choʻntak pulini boshqarmoq"],["develop saving habits","tejamkorlik odatini shakllantirmoq"]]},{"c":"4.10","p":false,"en":"Buying the latest models and paying for in-app purchases put a strain on the family budget.","uz":"Eng yangi modellarni sotib olish va ilova ichidagi xaridlar uchun toʻlash oila budjetiga ogʻirlik qiladi.","ch":[["the latest models","eng soʻnggi modellar"],["put a strain on the budget","budjetga ogʻirlik qilmoq"]]}]},{"n":5,"title":"Studying Abroad","uz":"Chet elda oʻqish","q":"More and more students choose to study abroad. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this trend.","ideas":[{"c":"5.1","p":true,"en":"Overcoming challenges alone boosts students’ self-confidence and makes them more resilient.","uz":"Qiyinchiliklarni yolgʻiz yengib oʻtish talabalarning oʻziga ishonchini oshiradi va ularni chidamliroq qiladi.","ch":[["boost self-confidence","oʻziga ishonchni oshirmoq"],["resilient","chidamli, matonatli"]]},{"c":"5.2","p":false,"en":"Many international students suffer from homesickness and find it hard to adapt to a new culture.","uz":"Koʻplab xalqaro talabalar Vatan sogʻinchidan qiynaladi va yangi madaniyatga moslashishni qiyin deb topadi.","ch":[["suffer from homesickness","Vatan sogʻinchidan qiynalmoq"],["find it hard to adapt","moslashishni qiyin deb topmoq"]]},{"c":"5.3","p":true,"en":"Studying in a foreign language sharpens language skills and opens up new ways of thinking.","uz":"Chet tilida oʻqish til koʻnikmalarini charxlaydi va fikrlashning yangi usullarini ochib beradi.","ch":[["sharpen language skills","til koʻnikmalarini charxlamoq"],["open up new ways of thinking","yangi fikrlash usullarini ochmoq"]]},{"c":"5.4","p":false,"en":"Adjusting to unfamiliar teaching methods can cause academic stress and mental exhaustion.","uz":"Notanish oʻqitish usullariga koʻnikish akademik stress va ruhiy charchoqni keltirib chiqarishi mumkin.","ch":[["cause academic stress","akademik stress keltirib chiqarmoq"],["mental exhaustion","ruhiy charchoq"]]},{"c":"5.5","p":true,"en":"Living independently pushes students to cook for themselves, so they tend to adopt healthier eating habits.","uz":"Mustaqil yashash talabalarni oʻzi uchun ovqat pishirishga undaydi, shuning uchun ular sogʻlomroq ovqatlanish odatlarini oʻzlashtirishga moyil boʻladi.","ch":[["cook for oneself","oʻzi uchun ovqat pishirmoq"],["adopt healthier eating habits","sogʻlom ovqatlanish odatlarini oʻzlashtirmoq"]]},{"c":"5.6","p":false,"en":"Irregular meals, poor sleep and a heavy workload can take a toll on students’ health.","uz":"Tartibsiz ovqatlanish, kam uyqu va katta oʻquv yuklamasi talabalarning sogʻligʻiga salbiy ta’sir qiladi.","ch":[["heavy workload","katta yuklama"],["take a toll on","...ga salbiy ta’sir qilmoq"]]},{"c":"5.7","p":true,"en":"Students make lifelong friends from different backgrounds and build an international network.","uz":"Talabalar turli muhitdan umrbod doʻstlar orttiradi va xalqaro aloqalar tarmogʻini shakllantiradi.","ch":[["make lifelong friends","umrbod doʻstlar orttirmoq"],["build an international network","xalqaro aloqalar tarmogʻini yaratmoq"]]},{"c":"5.8","p":false,"en":"Living far from home means drifting away from family and missing important events such as weddings.","uz":"Uydan uzoqda yashash oiladan uzoqlashish va toʻy kabi muhim tadbirlarni oʻtkazib yuborish demakdir.","ch":[["drift away from family","oiladan uzoqlashmoq"],["miss important events","muhim tadbirlarni oʻtkazib yubormoq"]]},{"c":"5.9","p":true,"en":"A foreign degree boosts employability and gives graduates access to better-paid jobs.","uz":"Chet el diplomi ish topish imkoniyatini oshiradi va bitiruvchilarga yaxshiroq maosh toʻlanadigan ishlarga yoʻl ochadi.","ch":[["boost employability","ish topish imkoniyatini oshirmoq"],["access to better-paid jobs","yuqori maoshli ishlarga yoʻl"]]},{"c":"5.10","p":false,"en":"Tuition fees and living expenses put a heavy burden on families, who may fall into debt.","uz":"Oʻqish toʻlovi va yashash xarajatlari oilalarga katta yuk boʻladi, ular qarzga botishi ham mumkin.","ch":[["tuition fees","oʻqish toʻlovi"],["fall into debt","qarzga botmoq"]]}]},{"n":6,"title":"International Tourism","uz":"Xalqaro turizm","q":"International tourism has brought both benefits and problems to many countries. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"6.1","p":true,"en":"Travelling lets people escape their daily routine and return refreshed.","uz":"Sayohat odamlarga kundalik tartibdan qochish va tetik boʻlib qaytish imkonini beradi.","ch":[["escape daily routine","kundalik tartibdan qochmoq"],["return refreshed","tetik boʻlib qaytmoq"]]},{"c":"6.2","p":false,"en":"Unexpected problems such as lost luggage can cause a great deal of stress and ruin the trip.","uz":"Yoʻqolgan yuk kabi kutilmagan muammolar katta stress keltirib chiqarishi va sayohatni buzib yuborishi mumkin.","ch":[["cause a great deal of stress","katta stress keltirib chiqarmoq"],["ruin the trip","sayohatni barbod qilmoq"]]},{"c":"6.3","p":true,"en":"Experiencing other cultures broadens one’s mind and helps people challenge stereotypes.","uz":"Boshqa madaniyatlarni oʻz koʻzi bilan koʻrish fikrlash doirasini kengaytiradi va stereotiplarni rad etishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["broaden one’s mind","fikrlash doirasini kengaytirmoq"],["challenge stereotypes","stereotiplarga qarshi chiqmoq"]]},{"c":"6.4","p":false,"en":"Travellers may suffer from culture shock and feel overwhelmed by unfamiliar surroundings.","uz":"Sayyohlar madaniy shokni boshdan kechirishi va notanish muhitdan boshi qotib qolishi mumkin.","ch":[["suffer from culture shock","madaniy shokni boshdan kechirmoq"],["feel overwhelmed","boshi qotib qolmoq"]]},{"c":"6.5","p":true,"en":"Hiking and exploring on foot help tourists stay physically active and enjoy the fresh air.","uz":"Piyoda yurish va sayohat qilish sayyohlarga jismonan faol boʻlib qolish va toza havodan bahramand boʻlishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["stay physically active","jismonan faol boʻlib turmoq"],["enjoy the fresh air","toza havodan bahramand boʻlmoq"]]},{"c":"6.6","p":false,"en":"Tourists risk catching an infection or suffering from food poisoning when they try unfamiliar food.","uz":"Notanish taomni tatib koʻrganda sayyohlar infeksiya yuqtirishi yoki ovqatdan zaharlanishi mumkin.","ch":[["catch an infection","infeksiya yuqtirmoq"],["suffer from food poisoning","ovqatdan zaharlanmoq"]]},{"c":"6.7","p":true,"en":"Travel allows people to meet locals and form lasting friendships across cultures.","uz":"Sayohat odamlarga mahalliy aholi bilan tanishish va madaniyatlar oraligʻida uzoq davom etadigan doʻstlik oʻrnatish imkonini beradi.","ch":[["meet locals","mahalliy aholi bilan tanishmoq"],["form lasting friendships","uzoq davom etadigan doʻstlik oʻrnatmoq"]]},{"c":"6.8","p":false,"en":"Mass tourism can cause overcrowding and erode local traditions, which annoys residents.","uz":"Ommaviy turizm gavjumlikni keltirib chiqarishi va mahalliy an’analarni yemirishi mumkin, bu esa aholini norozi qiladi.","ch":[["cause overcrowding","gavjumlikni keltirib chiqarmoq"],["erode local traditions","mahalliy an’analarni yemirmoq"]]},{"c":"6.9","p":true,"en":"Tourism creates thousands of jobs and boosts the local economy.","uz":"Turizm minglab ish oʻrinlari yaratadi va mahalliy iqtisodiyotni jonlantiradi.","ch":[["create jobs","ish oʻrinlari yaratmoq"],["boost the local economy","mahalliy iqtisodiyotni jonlantirmoq"]]},{"c":"6.10","p":false,"en":"Housing and food prices often soar in tourist areas, making life unaffordable for locals.","uz":"Turistik hududlarda uy-joy va oziq-ovqat narxlari koʻpincha keskin oshadi, bu esa hayotni mahalliy aholining qoʻli yetmaydigan darajaga olib chiqadi.","ch":[["soar","keskin oshmoq"],["unaffordable for locals","mahalliy aholining qoʻli yetmaydigan"]]}]},{"n":7,"title":"Living in Big Cities","uz":"Katta shaharlarda yashash","q":"Some people prefer to live in big cities, while others prefer small towns. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"7.1","p":true,"en":"Cities offer entertainment and events that lift people’s spirits and keep boredom at bay.","uz":"Shaharlar odamlarning kayfiyatini koʻtaradigan va zerikishning oldini oladigan koʻngilochar tadbirlar taklif qiladi.","ch":[["lift one’s spirits","kayfiyatni koʻtarmoq"],["keep boredom at bay","zerikishning oldini olmoq"]]},{"c":"7.2","p":false,"en":"The fast pace of life makes many residents feel anxious and under constant pressure.","uz":"Hayotning shiddatli sur’ati koʻp aholini xavotirga solib, doimiy bosim ostida ushlab turadi.","ch":[["the fast pace of life","hayotning shiddatli sur’ati"],["under constant pressure","doimiy bosim ostida"]]},{"c":"7.3","p":true,"en":"Access to libraries and cultural venues helps residents keep learning and stay intellectually stimulated.","uz":"Kutubxonalar va madaniy maskanlarga kirish imkoni aholiga oʻrganishda davom etish va aqlan faol boʻlib turishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["keep learning","oʻrganishda davom etmoq"],["stay intellectually stimulated","aqlan faol boʻlib turmoq"]]},{"c":"7.4","p":false,"en":"Noise, crowds and traffic jams wear people down and harm their mental health.","uz":"Shovqin, olomon va tirbandlik odamni toliqtiradi va ruhiy salomatligiga zarar yetkazadi.","ch":[["wear people down","odamni toliqtirib qoʻymoq"],["harm mental health","ruhiy salomatlikka zarar yetkazmoq"]]},{"c":"7.5","p":true,"en":"Hospitals and clinics are easily accessible, so residents can receive quick medical care.","uz":"Kasalxona va klinikalarga oson yetib boriladi, shuning uchun aholi tezkor tibbiy yordam ola oladi.","ch":[["easily accessible","oson yetib boriladigan"],["receive medical care","tibbiy yordam olmoq"]]},{"c":"7.6","p":false,"en":"Air pollution and heavy traffic increase the risk of respiratory problems.","uz":"Havoning ifloslanishi va qattiq tirbandlik nafas yoʻllari kasalliklari xavfini oshiradi.","ch":[["increase the risk of","...xavfini oshirmoq"],["respiratory problems","nafas yoʻllari kasalliklari"]]},{"c":"7.7","p":true,"en":"Cities bring together people from all walks of life, which helps residents widen their social circle.","uz":"Shaharlar turli qatlam vakillarini birlashtiradi, bu esa aholiga ijtimoiy doirasini kengaytirishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["from all walks of life","turli qatlam vakillari"],["widen one’s social circle","ijtimoiy doirani kengaytirmoq"]]},{"c":"7.8","p":false,"en":"Despite living among millions, many people feel anonymous and have little sense of community.","uz":"Millionlar orasida yashasa ham, koʻpchilik oʻzini begonadek his qiladi va jamoaga mansublik tuygʻusi kam boʻladi.","ch":[["feel anonymous","oʻzini begonadek his qilmoq"],["a sense of community","jamoaga mansublik tuygʻusi"]]},{"c":"7.9","p":true,"en":"Cities provide a wide range of job opportunities and higher salaries.","uz":"Shaharlar keng ish imkoniyatlari va yuqoriroq maosh taklif qiladi.","ch":[["a wide range of job opportunities","keng ish imkoniyatlari"],["higher salaries","yuqoriroq maosh"]]},{"c":"7.10","p":false,"en":"The cost of living is high, so rent and bills eat up most of people’s income.","uz":"Yashash narxi yuqori, shuning uchun ijara va kommunal toʻlovlar daromadning katta qismini yeb ketadi.","ch":[["the cost of living","yashash narxi"],["eat up","yeb qoʻymoq"]]}]},{"n":8,"title":"Video Games","uz":"Video oʻyinlar","q":"Some people believe video games are harmful to young people. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","ideas":[{"c":"8.1","p":true,"en":"Video games help players relieve stress and unwind after a long day.","uz":"Video oʻyinlar oʻyinchilarga stressdan xalos boʻlish va uzoq kundan keyin dam olishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["relieve stress","stressdan xalos boʻlmoq"],["unwind","dam olib tinchlanmoq"]]},{"c":"8.2","p":false,"en":"Losing repeatedly can trigger frustration, and some players become addicted.","uz":"Qayta-qayta yutqazish jahl va tushkunlikni qoʻzgʻatishi mumkin, ba’zi oʻyinchilar esa oʻyinga qaram boʻlib qoladi.","ch":[["trigger frustration","tushkunlikni qoʻzgʻatmoq"],["become addicted","qaram boʻlib qolmoq"]]},{"c":"8.3","p":true,"en":"Strategy games sharpen critical thinking and teach players to make quick decisions.","uz":"Strategik oʻyinlar tanqidiy fikrlashni charxlaydi va oʻyinchilarga tezkor qaror qabul qilishni oʻrgatadi.","ch":[["sharpen critical thinking","tanqidiy fikrlashni charxlamoq"],["make quick decisions","tezkor qaror qabul qilmoq"]]},{"c":"8.4","p":false,"en":"Players may lose track of time and neglect their studies.","uz":"Oʻyinchilar vaqtni unutib qoʻyishi va oʻqishini e’tiborsiz qoldirishi mumkin.","ch":[["lose track of time","vaqtni unutib qoʻymoq"],["neglect one’s studies","oʻqishni e’tiborsiz qoldirmoq"]]},{"c":"8.5","p":true,"en":"Motion-based games get players moving and improve hand-eye coordination.","uz":"Harakatga asoslangan oʻyinlar oʻyinchilarni harakatga keltiradi va qoʻl-koʻz muvofiqligini yaxshilaydi.","ch":[["get players moving","oʻyinchilarni harakatga keltirmoq"],["hand-eye coordination","qoʻl-koʻz muvofiqligi"]]},{"c":"8.6","p":false,"en":"Hours of sitting can lead to weight gain and weakened eyesight.","uz":"Soatlab oʻtirish ortiqcha vazn orttirishga va koʻrish qobiliyatining susayishiga olib kelishi mumkin.","ch":[["weight gain","vazn ortishi"],["weakened eyesight","susaygan koʻrish qobiliyati"]]},{"c":"8.7","p":true,"en":"Multiplayer games bring friends together and teach players how to work as a team.","uz":"Koʻp oʻyinchili oʻyinlar doʻstlarni jipslashtiradi va oʻyinchilarga jamoa boʻlib ishlashni oʻrgatadi.","ch":[["bring people together","odamlarni jipslashtirmoq"],["work as a team","jamoa boʻlib ishlamoq"]]},{"c":"8.8","p":false,"en":"Gamers may withdraw from real-life activities and lose touch with friends and family.","uz":"Geymerlar real hayotdagi faoliyatdan chetlashib, doʻst va oilasi bilan aloqani yoʻqotishi mumkin.","ch":[["withdraw from","...dan chetlashmoq"],["lose touch with","...bilan aloqani yoʻqotmoq"]]},{"c":"8.9","p":true,"en":"Talented gamers can make a living by joining e-sports tournaments and streaming.","uz":"Iqtidorli geymerlar kibersport turnirlarida qatnashib va strim qilib kun koʻrishi mumkin.","ch":[["make a living","kun koʻrmoq, tirikchilik qilmoq"],["e-sports tournament","kibersport turniri"]]},{"c":"8.10","p":false,"en":"In-game purchases and expensive consoles can drain players’ savings.","uz":"Oʻyin ichidagi xaridlar va qimmat konsollar oʻyinchilarning jamgʻarmasini tugatib qoʻyishi mumkin.","ch":[["in-game purchases","oʻyin ichidagi xaridlar"],["drain savings","jamgʻarmani tugatmoq"]]}]},{"n":9,"title":"Artificial Intelligence","uz":"Sun’iy intellekt","q":"Artificial intelligence is replacing humans in many areas of life. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"9.1","p":true,"en":"AI tools take over repetitive tasks, so people feel less overwhelmed at work.","uz":"SI vositalari takroriy ishlarni oʻz zimmasiga oladi, shuning uchun odamlar ishda oʻzini kamroq bosim ostida his qiladi.","ch":[["take over repetitive tasks","takroriy ishlarni oʻz zimmasiga olmoq"],["feel overwhelmed","bosim ostida qolgandek his qilmoq"]]},{"c":"9.2","p":false,"en":"Fear of being replaced by machines makes many workers feel insecure and anxious about the future.","uz":"Mashinalar oʻrnini egallashidan qoʻrqish koʻp ishchilarni ishonchsiz his qilishga va kelajak haqida xavotirga solmoqda.","ch":[["feel insecure","oʻzini ishonchsiz his qilmoq"],["anxious about the future","kelajak haqida xavotirda"]]},{"c":"9.3","p":true,"en":"AI tutors personalise lessons and explain difficult topics step by step.","uz":"SI repetitorlar darslarni har bir oʻquvchiga moslab, murakkab mavzularni bosqichma-bosqich tushuntiradi.","ch":[["personalise lessons","darslarni har kimga moslamoq"],["step by step","bosqichma-bosqich"]]},{"c":"9.4","p":false,"en":"Relying too much on AI can weaken critical thinking and encourage mental laziness.","uz":"SIga haddan ortiq tayanish tanqidiy fikrlashni susaytirishi va aqliy dangasalikni kuchaytirishi mumkin.","ch":[["rely on","...ga tayanmoq"],["weaken critical thinking","tanqidiy fikrlashni susaytirmoq"]]},{"c":"9.5","p":true,"en":"AI-assisted diagnosis helps doctors detect diseases early and save lives.","uz":"SI yordamidagi tashxis shifokorlarga kasalliklarni erta aniqlash va jonlarni asrab qolishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["detect diseases early","kasalliklarni erta aniqlamoq"],["save lives","jonlarni asrab qolmoq"]]},{"c":"9.6","p":false,"en":"When machines handle chores and errands, people move less and lead an inactive life, which harms their fitness.","uz":"Mashinalar uy ishlari va yumushlarni bajarganda, odamlar kam harakat qilib, harakatsiz hayot kechiradi va bu jismoniy tayyorgarligiga zarar yetkazadi.","ch":[["lead an inactive life","harakatsiz hayot kechirmoq"],["harm one’s fitness","jismoniy tayyorgarlikka zarar yetkazmoq"]]},{"c":"9.7","p":true,"en":"AI translation tools break down language barriers and help people communicate across cultures.","uz":"SI tarjima vositalari til toʻsiqlarini yoʻq qiladi va odamlarga madaniyatlararo muloqot qilishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["break down language barriers","til toʻsiqlarini yoʻq qilmoq"],["communicate across cultures","madaniyatlararo muloqot qilmoq"]]},{"c":"9.8","p":false,"en":"Chatbots may replace human contact, leaving people less skilled at real conversations.","uz":"Chatbotlar insonlar oʻrtasidagi muloqotni almashtirib qoʻyishi mumkin, natijada odamlar jonli suhbatda kamroq mohir boʻlib qoladi.","ch":[["replace human contact","insoniy muloqotni almashtirmoq"],["real conversations","jonli suhbatlar"]]},{"c":"9.9","p":true,"en":"Automation cuts production costs and boosts company profits.","uz":"Avtomatlashtirish ishlab chiqarish xarajatlarini qisqartiradi va kompaniya foydasini oshiradi.","ch":[["cut costs","xarajatlarni qisqartirmoq"],["boost profits","foydani oshirmoq"]]},{"c":"9.10","p":false,"en":"Machines replace human workers, causing job losses and widening the income gap.","uz":"Mashinalar inson xodimlarning oʻrnini egallab, ish oʻrinlari yoʻqolishiga va daromadlar tafovutining kengayishiga sabab boʻladi.","ch":[["replace workers","xodimlarning oʻrnini egallamoq"],["widen the income gap","daromadlar tafovutini kengaytirmoq"]]}]},{"n":10,"title":"Online Shopping","uz":"Onlayn xarid","q":"Online shopping is replacing traditional shops. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"10.1","p":true,"en":"Buying gifts online lets people surprise their loved ones and avoid the stress of crowded stores.","uz":"Onlayn sovgʻa xarid qilish odamlarga yaqinlarini hayratga solish va gavjum doʻkonlar keltirib chiqaradigan stressdan qochish imkonini beradi.","ch":[["surprise loved ones","yaqinlarini hayratga solmoq"],["the stress of crowded stores","gavjum doʻkonlar keltiradigan stress"]]},{"c":"10.2","p":false,"en":"Buying things when feeling low brings only short-lived pleasure, and many shoppers feel guilty afterwards.","uz":"Kayfiyat tushkun paytda xarid qilish faqat qisqa muddatli zavq beradi, koʻp xaridorlar keyin oʻzini aybdor his qiladi.","ch":[["short-lived pleasure","qisqa muddatli zavq"],["feel guilty","oʻzini aybdor his qilmoq"]]},{"c":"10.3","p":true,"en":"Shoppers can compare prices and read reviews, so they make informed decisions.","uz":"Xaridorlar narxlarni solishtirib, sharhlarni oʻqiy oladi, shuning uchun ongli qaror qabul qiladi.","ch":[["compare prices","narxlarni solishtirmoq"],["make informed decisions","ongli qaror qabul qilmoq"]]},{"c":"10.4","p":false,"en":"Endless choices and flash sales create decision fatigue and pressure people into buying things they did not plan to.","uz":"Cheksiz tanlov va tezkor aksiyalar qaror qabul qilishdan charchashni keltirib chiqaradi va odamlarni rejalashtirmagan narsalarini sotib olishga undaydi.","ch":[["flash sale","qisqa muddatli chegirma aksiyasi"],["decision fatigue","qaror qabul qilishdan charchash"]]},{"c":"10.5","p":true,"en":"Home delivery helps people with limited mobility avoid carrying heavy bags.","uz":"Uyga yetkazib berish harakati cheklangan odamlarga ogʻir sumkalarni koʻtarishdan qutulishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["limited mobility","cheklangan harakatchanlik"],["avoid carrying heavy bags","ogʻir sumkalarni koʻtarishdan qutulmoq"]]},{"c":"10.6","p":false,"en":"Shopping from the sofa means people get less exercise and spend more time sitting.","uz":"Divandan turib xarid qilish odamlar kamroq harakat qilishi va koʻproq oʻtirishini anglatadi.","ch":[["get less exercise","kamroq harakat qilmoq"],["spend time sitting","oʻtirib vaqt oʻtkazmoq"]]},{"c":"10.7","p":true,"en":"Busy parents enjoy quality time with their children because they avoid spending hours in malls.","uz":"Band ota-onalar bolalari bilan sifatli vaqt oʻtkazadi, chunki savdo markazlarida soatlab aylanib yurishmaydi.","ch":[["quality time with children","bolalar bilan sifatli vaqt"],["spend hours in malls","savdo markazlarida soatlab vaqt oʻtkazmoq"]]},{"c":"10.8","p":false,"en":"People no longer meet neighbours at local shops, so community ties begin to weaken.","uz":"Odamlar mahalla doʻkonlarida qoʻshnilari bilan uchrashmaydi, shuning uchun mahalla aloqalari susayib boradi.","ch":[["community ties","mahalla aloqalari"],["weaken","susaymoq"]]},{"c":"10.9","p":true,"en":"Online stores offer big discounts and free delivery, helping shoppers cut their spending.","uz":"Onlayn doʻkonlar katta chegirmalar va bepul yetkazib berish taklif qilib, xaridorlarning xarajatini kamaytiradi.","ch":[["offer big discounts","katta chegirmalar taklif qilmoq"],["free delivery","bepul yetkazib berish"]]},{"c":"10.10","p":false,"en":"Hidden fees and impulse purchases can empty people’s wallets.","uz":"Yashirin toʻlovlar va oʻylamasdan qilingan xaridlar odamlarning hamyonini boʻshatib qoʻyishi mumkin.","ch":[["hidden fees","yashirin toʻlovlar"],["empty one’s wallet","hamyonni boʻshatmoq"]]}]},{"n":11,"title":"Fast Food","uz":"Fast-fud (tez ovqat)","q":"Fast food has become a part of modern life. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"11.1","p":true,"en":"A tasty burger after a tough day can lift one’s mood and bring instant comfort.","uz":"Ogʻir kundan keyin mazali burger kayfiyatni koʻtarib, bir zumda taskin beradi.","ch":[["lift one’s mood","kayfiyatni koʻtarmoq"],["instant comfort","bir zumda taskin"]]},{"c":"11.2","p":false,"en":"People who eat junk food regularly often feel guilty and unhappy with their body image.","uz":"Muntazam fast-fud yeydiganlar koʻpincha oʻzini aybdor his qiladi va oʻz tanasidan norozi boʻladi.","ch":[["feel guilty","oʻzini aybdor his qilmoq"],["body image","oʻz tanasi haqidagi tasavvur"]]},{"c":"11.3","p":true,"en":"Quick meals save time and effort, so busy people can focus on their work.","uz":"Tez tayyor ovqat vaqt va kuchni tejaydi, shuning uchun band odamlar ishiga e’tibor qarata oladi.","ch":[["save time and effort","vaqt va kuchni tejamoq"],["focus on work","ishga e’tibor qaratmoq"]]},{"c":"11.4","p":false,"en":"Food high in sugar and fat can cause energy crashes and brain fog.","uz":"Shakar va yogʻi koʻp ovqat quvvatning keskin tushishi va fikrlarning xiralashishiga sabab boʻlishi mumkin.","ch":[["energy crash","quvvatning keskin tushishi"],["brain fog","fikrlarning xiralashishi"]]},{"c":"11.5","p":true,"en":"Many chains now offer healthier options, so customers can keep a balanced diet.","uz":"Koʻplab tarmoqlar endi sogʻlomroq tanlovlar taklif qiladi, shuning uchun mijozlar muvozanatli ovqatlanishni saqlay oladi.","ch":[["healthier options","sogʻlomroq tanlovlar"],["keep a balanced diet","muvozanatli ovqatlanishni saqlamoq"]]},{"c":"11.6","p":false,"en":"Regular consumption leads to obesity and increases the risk of heart disease.","uz":"Muntazam iste’mol qilish semirishga olib keladi va yurak kasalliklari xavfini oshiradi.","ch":[["lead to obesity","semirishga olib kelmoq"],["heart disease","yurak kasalliklari"]]},{"c":"11.7","p":true,"en":"Fast-food restaurants are popular meeting spots where friends can get together on a budget.","uz":"Fast-fud restoranlari doʻstlar arzon narxda yigʻiladigan ommabop uchrashuv joylaridir.","ch":[["popular meeting spot","ommabop uchrashuv joyi"],["get together","yigʻilmoq"]]},{"c":"11.8","p":false,"en":"Grabbing a burger on the go means families rarely eat together, which weakens family bonds.","uz":"Yoʻl-yoʻlakay burger yeyish oilalar kamdan-kam birga ovqatlanishini anglatadi, bu esa oilaviy rishtalarni susaytiradi.","ch":[["eat together","birga ovqatlanmoq"],["weaken family bonds","oilaviy rishtalarni susaytirmoq"]]},{"c":"11.9","p":true,"en":"Fast food is cheap and filling, so people on a tight budget can eat out affordably.","uz":"Fast-fud arzon va toʻyimli, shuning uchun mablagʻi cheklangan odamlar ham arzon narxda tashqarida ovqatlana oladi.","ch":[["cheap and filling","arzon va toʻyimli"],["on a tight budget","mablagʻi cheklangan"]]},{"c":"11.10","p":false,"en":"In the long run, medical bills for diet-related diseases cost far more than healthy meals.","uz":"Uzoq muddatda ovqatlanish bilan bogʻliq kasalliklarni davolash xarajatlari sogʻlom ovqatdan ancha qimmatga tushadi.","ch":[["in the long run","uzoq muddatda"],["medical bills","davolanish xarajatlari"]]}]},{"n":12,"title":"Team Sports","uz":"Jamoaviy sport","q":"Some people think children should play team sports at school. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"12.1","p":true,"en":"Winning together boosts self-esteem and gives players a sense of belonging.","uz":"Birgalikda gʻalaba qozonish oʻziga hurmatni oshiradi va oʻyinchilarga jamoaga mansublik hissini beradi.","ch":[["boost self-esteem","oʻziga hurmatni oshirmoq"],["a sense of belonging","jamoaga mansublik hissi"]]},{"c":"12.2","p":false,"en":"Losing important matches can leave players feeling disappointed and under intense pressure.","uz":"Muhim oʻyinlarda yutqazish oʻyinchilarni hafsalasi pir boʻlgan holatda va qattiq bosim ostida qoldirishi mumkin.","ch":[["feel disappointed","hafsalasi pir boʻlmoq"],["under intense pressure","qattiq bosim ostida"]]},{"c":"12.3","p":true,"en":"Team sports teach players to think strategically and stay disciplined.","uz":"Jamoaviy sport oʻyinchilarga strategik fikrlashni va intizomli boʻlishni oʻrgatadi.","ch":[["think strategically","strategik fikrlamoq"],["stay disciplined","intizomli boʻlib qolmoq"]]},{"c":"12.4","p":false,"en":"Heavy training schedules leave little time for studying and can cause burnout.","uz":"Ogʻir mashgʻulot jadvali oʻqishga juda oz vaqt qoldiradi va holdan toyishga sabab boʻlishi mumkin.","ch":[["leave little time for","...ga juda oz vaqt qoldirmoq"],["burnout","holdan toyish"]]},{"c":"12.5","p":true,"en":"Regular training builds stamina and helps young people stay in shape.","uz":"Muntazam mashgʻulotlar chidamlilikni oshiradi va yoshlarga formada qolishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["build stamina","chidamlilikni oshirmoq"],["stay in shape","formada qolmoq"]]},{"c":"12.6","p":false,"en":"Contact sports raise the risk of sprains and fractures and long-term injuries.","uz":"Kontaktli sport turlari choʻzilish, suyak sinishi va uzoq muddatli jarohatlar xavfini oshiradi.","ch":[["sprains and fractures","choʻzilish va suyak sinishlari"],["long-term injury","uzoq muddatli jarohat"]]},{"c":"12.7","p":true,"en":"Players learn to cooperate and foster team spirit, which helps them in adult life.","uz":"Oʻyinchilar hamkorlik qilishni oʻrganadi va jamoaviy ruhni mustahkamlaydi, bu ularga katta boʻlganda ham yordam beradi.","ch":[["learn to cooperate","hamkorlik qilishni oʻrganmoq"],["foster team spirit","jamoaviy ruhni mustahkamlamoq"]]},{"c":"12.8","p":false,"en":"Fierce rivalry can spark conflict among teammates, and weaker players may be left out.","uz":"Qattiq raqobat jamoadoshlar oʻrtasida nizo chiqarishi va kuchsizroq oʻyinchilar chetda qolishi mumkin.","ch":[["spark conflict","nizo qoʻzgʻatmoq"],["be left out","chetda qolmoq"]]},{"c":"12.9","p":true,"en":"Talented athletes can win scholarships and launch professional careers.","uz":"Iqtidorli sportchilar stipendiya yutib, professional karyerasini boshlashi mumkin.","ch":[["win a scholarship","stipendiya yutmoq"],["launch a career","karyera boshlamoq"]]},{"c":"12.10","p":false,"en":"Equipment, travel and membership fees add up quickly for families.","uz":"Jihozlar, yoʻlkira va a’zolik toʻlovlari oilalar uchun tez koʻpayib ketadi.","ch":[["membership fees","a’zolik toʻlovlari"],["add up","toʻplanib koʻpayib ketmoq"]]}]},{"n":13,"title":"Learning Foreign Languages","uz":"Chet tillarini oʻrganish","q":"Learning a foreign language is more important than ever. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","ideas":[{"c":"13.1","p":true,"en":"Speaking a foreign language boosts confidence and gives learners a sense of achievement.","uz":"Chet tilida gapirish ishonchni oshiradi va oʻrganuvchilarga erishilgan yutuq hissini beradi.","ch":[["boost confidence","ishonchni oshirmoq"],["a sense of achievement","yutuq hissi"]]},{"c":"13.2","p":false,"en":"Making mistakes in front of others can make learners feel embarrassed and give up.","uz":"Boshqalar oldida xato qilish oʻrganuvchilarni xijolat qilib, voz kechishga undashi mumkin.","ch":[["feel embarrassed","xijolat boʻlmoq"],["give up","voz kechmoq"]]},{"c":"13.3","p":true,"en":"Bilingual people tend to improve their memory and switch between tasks more easily.","uz":"Ikki tilli odamlar xotirasini yaxshilashga va vazifalar oʻrtasida osonroq oʻta olishga moyil boʻladi.","ch":[["improve memory","xotirani yaxshilamoq"],["switch between tasks","vazifalar oʻrtasida almashmoq"]]},{"c":"13.4","p":false,"en":"Learners often hit a plateau after months of study, which can be frustrating.","uz":"Oʻrganuvchilar bir necha oy oʻqigandan keyin koʻpincha rivojlanishda toʻxtab qoladi, bu esa jahlni chiqarishi mumkin.","ch":[["hit a plateau","rivojlanishda toʻxtab qolmoq"],["frustrating","jahlni chiqaradigan"]]},{"c":"13.5","p":true,"en":"Learning languages keeps the brain healthy and delays age-related decline.","uz":"Til oʻrganish miyani sogʻlom saqlaydi va yoshga bogʻliq pasayishni kechiktiradi.","ch":[["keep the brain healthy","miyani sogʻlom saqlamoq"],["delay age-related decline","yoshga bogʻliq pasayishni kechiktirmoq"]]},{"c":"13.6","p":false,"en":"Staying up late to study can lead to sleep deprivation and eye strain.","uz":"Tunni oʻqib oʻtkazish uyqusizlikka va koʻz charchashiga olib kelishi mumkin.","ch":[["stay up late","kech yotmoq, tunni oʻtkazmoq"],["sleep deprivation","uyqusizlik"]]},{"c":"13.7","p":true,"en":"Language skills help people communicate with foreigners and gain cultural insight.","uz":"Til bilish odamlarga chet elliklar bilan muloqot qilish va madaniyatni chuqurroq tushunishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["communicate with foreigners","chet elliklar bilan muloqot qilmoq"],["gain cultural insight","madaniyatni chuqurroq anglamoq"]]},{"c":"13.8","p":false,"en":"Some learners feel left out when speaking with fluent speakers, so they avoid social situations.","uz":"Ba’zi oʻrganuvchilar ravon soʻzlashuvchilar bilan gaplashganda oʻzini chetda qolgandek his qiladi va ijtimoiy vaziyatlardan qochadi.","ch":[["feel left out","oʻzini chetda qolgandek his qilmoq"],["avoid social situations","ijtimoiy vaziyatlardan qochmoq"]]},{"c":"13.9","p":true,"en":"Fluent speakers earn higher salaries and have a competitive edge in the job market.","uz":"Ravon soʻzlashuvchilar yuqoriroq maosh oladi va mehnat bozorida raqobatda ustunlikka ega boʻladi.","ch":[["earn higher salaries","yuqoriroq maosh olmoq"],["have a competitive edge","raqobatda ustunlikka ega boʻlmoq"]]},{"c":"13.10","p":false,"en":"Private courses, textbooks and exams cost a fortune, so many learners cannot afford them.","uz":"Xususiy kurslar, darsliklar va imtihonlar juda qimmatga tushadi, shuning uchun koʻp oʻrganuvchilarning qoʻli yetmaydi.","ch":[["cost a fortune","juda qimmatga tushmoq"],["cannot afford","qoʻli yetmaydi"]]}]},{"n":14,"title":"Homework","uz":"Uy vazifasi","q":"Some people think children should be given homework every day. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"14.1","p":true,"en":"Completing assignments gives pupils a sense of accomplishment and helps them take pride in their work.","uz":"Topshiriqlarni bajarish oʻquvchilarga qilingan ish hissini beradi va oʻz mehnatidan faxrlanishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["a sense of accomplishment","bajarilgan ish hissi"],["take pride in","...dan faxrlanmoq"]]},{"c":"14.2","p":false,"en":"A mountain of homework causes anxiety and makes pupils dread school.","uz":"Uy vazifasi togʻi xavotir keltirib chiqaradi va oʻquvchilarni maktabdan choʻchitadi.","ch":[["a mountain of homework","uy vazifasi togʻi"],["dread school","maktabdan choʻchimoq"]]},{"c":"14.3","p":true,"en":"Homework helps students reinforce what they have learned and develop self-discipline.","uz":"Uy vazifasi oʻquvchilarga oʻrganganlarini mustahkamlashga va oʻzini boshqarishni rivojlantirishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["reinforce learning","bilimni mustahkamlamoq"],["develop self-discipline","oʻzini boshqarishni rivojlantirmoq"]]},{"c":"14.4","p":false,"en":"Overloaded pupils often copy answers just to meet deadlines, which defeats the purpose.","uz":"Yuklama koʻp boʻlgan oʻquvchilar muddatga ulgurish uchun koʻpincha javoblarni koʻchiradi, bu esa maqsadga ziddir.","ch":[["copy answers","javoblarni koʻchirmoq"],["meet deadlines","muddatga ulgurmoq"]]},{"c":"14.5","p":true,"en":"Practical assignments get kids outdoors and give them hands-on experience.","uz":"Amaliy topshiriqlar bolalarni ochiq havoga olib chiqadi va ularga amaliy tajriba beradi.","ch":[["get kids outdoors","bolalarni ochiq havoga chiqarmoq"],["hands-on experience","amaliy tajriba"]]},{"c":"14.6","p":false,"en":"Finishing assignments late at night means pupils cut down on sleep and have no time for exercise.","uz":"Topshiriqlarni tunda tugatish oʻquvchilar uyqusini qisqartirishi va sport uchun vaqti qolmasligini anglatadi.","ch":[["cut down on sleep","uyqusini qisqartirmoq"],["no time for exercise","sport uchun vaqt yoʻq"]]},{"c":"14.7","p":true,"en":"Group assignments teach students to share responsibilities, and parents can get involved in their children’s learning.","uz":"Guruhli topshiriqlar oʻquvchilarga mas’uliyatni boʻlishishni oʻrgatadi, ota-onalar esa bolalarining oʻqishida ishtirok etishi mumkin.","ch":[["share responsibilities","mas’uliyatni boʻlishmoq"],["get involved in","...da ishtirok etmoq"]]},{"c":"14.8","p":false,"en":"Heavy homework eats into family time and leaves children no time to hang out with friends.","uz":"Koʻp uy vazifasi oila vaqtini yeb qoʻyadi va bolalarga doʻstlari bilan vaqt oʻtkazishga imkon qoldirmaydi.","ch":[["eat into family time","oila vaqtini kamaytirmoq"],["hang out with friends","doʻstlar bilan vaqt oʻtkazmoq"]]},{"c":"14.9","p":true,"en":"Strong study habits lead to better grades, which open doors to scholarships.","uz":"Kuchli oʻqish odatlari yaxshiroq baholarga olib keladi, bu esa stipendiyalarga eshik ochadi.","ch":[["lead to better grades","yaxshiroq baholarga olib kelmoq"],["open doors to","...ga eshik ochmoq"]]},{"c":"14.10","p":false,"en":"Families often hire a private tutor to help children keep up with the workload.","uz":"Oilalar bolalar yuklamaga ulgurishi uchun koʻpincha xususiy repetitor yollaydi.","ch":[["hire a private tutor","xususiy repetitor yollamoq"],["keep up with","...ga ulgurmoq, ortda qolmaslik"]]}]},{"n":15,"title":"Taking a Gap Year","uz":"Bir yillik tanaffus (gap year)","q":"Some young people take a year off before university. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"15.1","p":true,"en":"A year off helps young people recharge their batteries and return with fresh enthusiasm.","uz":"Bir yillik tanaffus yoshlarga kuch toʻplashga va yangi ishtiyoq bilan qaytishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["recharge one’s batteries","kuch toʻplamoq"],["fresh enthusiasm","yangi ishtiyoq"]]},{"c":"15.2","p":false,"en":"Watching friends move ahead can make gap-year takers feel left behind and lose confidence.","uz":"Doʻstlarining oldinga ketayotganini koʻrish tanaffus olganlarni ortda qolgandek his qilishga va ishonchini yoʻqotishga olib kelishi mumkin.","ch":[["feel left behind","ortda qolgandek his qilmoq"],["lose confidence","ishonchni yoʻqotmoq"]]},{"c":"15.3","p":true,"en":"Real-life experience helps teens discover their passions and choose a career path.","uz":"Hayotiy tajriba oʻsmirlarga qiziqishlarini kashf etish va kasb yoʻlini tanlashga yordam beradi.","ch":[["discover one’s passion","oʻz qiziqishini kashf etmoq"],["choose a career path","kasb yoʻlini tanlamoq"]]},{"c":"15.4","p":false,"en":"A long break may make students lose the habit of studying and struggle to get back into learning.","uz":"Uzoq tanaffus talabalarning oʻqish odatini yoʻqotishiga va oʻqishga qaytishda qiynalishiga sabab boʻlishi mumkin.","ch":[["lose the habit of studying","oʻqish odatini yoʻqotmoq"],["get back into","...ga qaytmoq"]]},{"c":"15.5","p":true,"en":"Outdoor volunteering and farm work keep young people physically active and spending time outdoors.","uz":"Ochiq havoda koʻngillilik va dehqonchilik ishlari yoshlarni jismonan faol saqlaydi va ochiq havoda koʻproq vaqt oʻtkazishga undaydi.","ch":[["physically active","jismonan faol"],["spend time outdoors","ochiq havoda vaqt oʻtkazmoq"]]},{"c":"15.6","p":false,"en":"Unsafe travel and poor accommodation expose young travellers to health and safety risks.","uz":"Xavfli sayohat va past sifatli turar joy yosh sayohatchilarni sogʻliq va xavfsizlik xatarlariga duchor qiladi.","ch":[["expose to","...ga duchor qilmoq"],["health and safety risks","sogʻliq va xavfsizlik xatarlari"]]},{"c":"15.7","p":true,"en":"Meeting people from different backgrounds helps youngsters develop social skills and become more open-minded.","uz":"Turli muhitdan kelgan odamlar bilan tanishish yoshlarga ijtimoiy koʻnikmalarni rivojlantirish va fikri kengroq boʻlishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["develop social skills","ijtimoiy koʻnikmalarni rivojlantirmoq"],["open-minded","fikri keng"]]},{"c":"15.8","p":false,"en":"After returning, they may feel out of place among younger classmates and be a year behind their friends.","uz":"Qaytgach, ular yoshroq sinfdoshlari orasida oʻzini begonadek his qilishi va doʻstlaridan bir yil ortda qolishi mumkin.","ch":[["feel out of place","oʻzini begonadek his qilmoq"],["be a year behind","bir yil ortda boʻlmoq"]]},{"c":"15.9","p":true,"en":"Part-time jobs during the break let them save up for tuition and learn to manage money.","uz":"Tanaffus davomidagi yarim kunlik ish ularga oʻqish toʻlovi uchun pul yigʻish va pulni boshqarishni oʻrganishga imkon beradi.","ch":[["save up for tuition","oʻqish toʻlovi uchun pul yigʻmoq"],["manage money","pulni boshqarmoq"]]},{"c":"15.10","p":false,"en":"A year without income delays entering the workforce and postpones earning a salary.","uz":"Daromadsiz oʻtgan bir yil mehnat bozoriga kirishni kechiktiradi va maosh olishni orqaga suradi.","ch":[["delay","kechiktirmoq"],["enter the workforce","mehnat bozoriga kirmoq"]]}]},{"n":16,"title":"Becoming Famous","uz":"Mashhur boʻlish","q":"Many young people want to become famous. Do the advantages of fame outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"16.1","p":true,"en":"Public admiration gives celebrities a sense of fulfilment and a feeling of purpose.","uz":"Ommaning e’tirofi mashhurlarga qoniqish hissini va hayot maqsadi tuygʻusini beradi.","ch":[["public admiration","ommaning e’tirofi"],["a sense of fulfilment","qoniqish hissi"]]},{"c":"16.2","p":false,"en":"Harsh criticism from fans can hurt celebrities deeply and push them into self-doubt.","uz":"Muxlislarning shafqatsiz tanqidi mashhurlarni qattiq ranjitishi va ularni oʻziga shubhaga solishi mumkin.","ch":[["hurt deeply","qattiq ranjitmoq"],["self-doubt","oʻziga shubha"]]},{"c":"16.3","p":true,"en":"Being in the spotlight pushes stars to keep learning and hone their skills.","uz":"E’tibor markazida boʻlish yulduzlarni oʻrganishda davom etishga va mahoratini charxlashga undaydi.","ch":[["in the spotlight","e’tibor markazida"],["keep learning","oʻrganishda davom etmoq"],["hone skills","mahoratini charxlamoq"]]},{"c":"16.4","p":false,"en":"Constant public attention creates pressure to be perfect, which can drain creativity.","uz":"Doimiy ommaviy e’tibor mukammal boʻlish bosimini yaratadi, bu esa ijodkorlikni soʻndirishi mumkin.","ch":[["pressure to be perfect","mukammal boʻlish bosimi"],["drain creativity","ijodkorlikni soʻndirmoq"]]},{"c":"16.5","p":true,"en":"Wealth lets stars hire personal trainers and access top-quality healthcare.","uz":"Boylik yulduzlarga shaxsiy murabbiy yollash va eng sifatli tibbiy xizmatdan foydalanish imkonini beradi.","ch":[["hire a personal trainer","shaxsiy murabbiy yollamoq"],["access top-quality healthcare","yuqori sifatli tibbiy xizmatdan foydalanmoq"]]},{"c":"16.6","p":false,"en":"Packed schedules and late-night events disrupt sleep and encourage unhealthy habits.","uz":"Gavjum jadval va tungi tadbirlar uyquni buzadi va nosogʻlom odatlarni kuchaytiradi.","ch":[["packed schedule","toʻla band jadval"],["disrupt sleep","uyquni buzmoq"]]},{"c":"16.7","p":true,"en":"Famous people can use their influence to raise awareness of social issues and inspire young people.","uz":"Mashhurlar oʻz ta’siridan foydalanib, ijtimoiy muammolar haqida xabardorlikni oshirishi va yoshlarga ilhom berishi mumkin.","ch":[["use one’s influence","oʻz ta’siridan foydalanmoq"],["raise awareness","xabardorlikni oshirmoq"]]},{"c":"16.8","p":false,"en":"Fame means celebrities lose their privacy and struggle to tell true friends from opportunists.","uz":"Shuhrat mashhurlar shaxsiy hayotidan mahrum boʻlishini va haqiqiy doʻstlarni foydaparastlardan ajratishda qiynalishini anglatadi.","ch":[["lose privacy","shaxsiy hayotdan mahrum boʻlmoq"],["tell true friends from opportunists","haqiqiy doʻstlarni foydaparastlardan ajratmoq"]]},{"c":"16.9","p":true,"en":"Famous people earn huge incomes through advertising and endorsement deals.","uz":"Mashhurlar reklama va reklama shartnomalari orqali katta daromad topadi.","ch":[["earn a huge income","katta daromad topmoq"],["endorsement deal","reklama shartnomasi"]]},{"c":"16.10","p":false,"en":"Many stars waste their fortunes and eventually go bankrupt.","uz":"Koʻp yulduzlar boyligini sovurib, oxir-oqibat bankrot boʻladi.","ch":[["waste a fortune","boylikni sovurmoq"],["go bankrupt","bankrot boʻlmoq"]]}]},{"n":17,"title":"Young Adults Living with Parents","uz":"Yoshlarning ota-onasi bilan yashashi","q":"More young adults are living with their parents. Is this a positive or negative development?","ideas":[{"c":"17.1","p":true,"en":"Living at home helps young adults feel loved and supported and gives them someone to turn to.","uz":"Uyda yashash yoshlarning oʻzini sevilgan va qoʻllab-quvvatlangandek his qilishiga yordam beradi va ularga murojaat qiladigan odam beradi.","ch":[["feel loved and supported","oʻzini sevilgan va qoʻllab-quvvatlangandek his qilmoq"],["someone to turn to","yordam soʻrab murojaat qiladigan odam"]]},{"c":"17.2","p":false,"en":"Parental control can make adult children feel dependent and resentful.","uz":"Ota-ona nazorati katta boʻlgan farzandlarni oʻzini qaram va ichida norozi his qilishga olib kelishi mumkin.","ch":[["feel dependent","oʻzini qaram his qilmoq"],["resentful","ichida alam, norozilik saqlagan"]]},{"c":"17.3","p":true,"en":"Advice from elders helps young people make wise decisions and learn from their experience.","uz":"Kattalarning maslahati yoshlarga oqilona qarorlar qabul qilish va ularning tajribasidan oʻrganishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["make wise decisions","oqilona qaror qabul qilmoq"],["learn from experience","tajribadan oʻrganmoq"]]},{"c":"17.4","p":false,"en":"Without independence, young adults fail to develop life skills and may not take responsibility for their choices.","uz":"Mustaqillik boʻlmasa, yoshlar hayotiy koʻnikmalarni rivojlantira olmaydi va oʻz tanlovi uchun mas’uliyat olmasligi mumkin.","ch":[["develop life skills","hayotiy koʻnikmalarni rivojlantirmoq"],["take responsibility for","...uchun mas’uliyat olmoq"]]},{"c":"17.5","p":true,"en":"Home-cooked meals mean young people eat a balanced diet more often.","uz":"Uyda pishirilgan ovqat yoshlarning muvozanatli ovqatlanishini koʻpaytiradi.","ch":[["home-cooked meals","uyda pishirilgan ovqat"],["eat a balanced diet","muvozanatli ovqatlanmoq"]]},{"c":"17.6","p":false,"en":"A crowded home with little personal space may disturb sleep and make it hard to rest.","uz":"Tor va gavjum uyda shaxsiy makon kam boʻladi, bu uyquni buzishi va dam olishni qiyinlashtirishi mumkin.","ch":[["personal space","shaxsiy makon"],["disturb sleep","uyquga xalaqit bermoq"]]},{"c":"17.7","p":true,"en":"Living together strengthens family bonds and lets young people look after elderly relatives.","uz":"Birga yashash oilaviy rishtalarni mustahkamlaydi va yoshlarga keksa qarindoshlariga qarashishga imkon beradi.","ch":[["strengthen family bonds","oilaviy rishtalarni mustahkamlamoq"],["look after elderly relatives","keksa qarindoshlarga qarashmoq"]]},{"c":"17.8","p":false,"en":"Disagreements over lifestyle cause friction and limit social freedom.","uz":"Turmush tarzi boʻyicha kelishmovchiliklar ziddiyat keltirib chiqaradi va ijtimoiy erkinlikni cheklaydi.","ch":[["cause friction","ziddiyat keltirib chiqarmoq"],["limit social freedom","ijtimoiy erkinlikni cheklamoq"]]},{"c":"17.9","p":true,"en":"Young adults can save on rent and put money aside for the future.","uz":"Yoshlar ijaradan tejab, kelajak uchun pul chetga qoʻya oladi.","ch":[["save on rent","ijara toʻlovini tejamoq"],["put money aside","pulni chetga qoʻymoq"]]},{"c":"17.10","p":false,"en":"Depending on parents for too long delays financial independence and puts pressure on the family budget.","uz":"Ota-onaga haddan ortiq uzoq qaram boʻlish moliyaviy mustaqillikni kechiktiradi va oila budjetiga bosim oʻtkazadi.","ch":[["delay financial independence","moliyaviy mustaqillikni kechiktirmoq"],["put pressure on","...ga bosim oʻtkazmoq"]]}]},{"n":18,"title":"Cashless Payments","uz":"Naqd pulsiz toʻlovlar","q":"Cash is being replaced by cards and mobile payments. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"18.1","p":true,"en":"Paying by phone gives shoppers peace of mind, as they no longer worry about carrying or losing cash.","uz":"Telefon orqali toʻlash xaridorlarga koʻngil xotirjamligini beradi, chunki ular naqd pulni olib yurish yoki yoʻqotishdan tashvishlanmaydi.","ch":[["peace of mind","koʻngil xotirjamligi"],["no longer worry about","...haqida endi tashvishlanmaslik"]]},{"c":"18.2","p":false,"en":"Hacked accounts and failed payments can cause panic and anxiety.","uz":"Buzib kirilgan hisoblar va muvaffaqiyatsiz toʻlovlar vahima va xavotir keltirib chiqarishi mumkin.","ch":[["hacked account","buzib kirilgan hisob"],["panic and anxiety","vahima va xavotir"]]},{"c":"18.3","p":true,"en":"Payment apps track spending automatically, so users plan their budgets more wisely.","uz":"Toʻlov ilovalari xarajatlarni avtomatik kuzatadi, shuning uchun foydalanuvchilar budjetini oqilonaroq rejalashtiradi.","ch":[["track spending","xarajatlarni kuzatmoq"],["plan a budget","budjetni rejalashtirmoq"]]},{"c":"18.4","p":false,"en":"Digital money feels painless to spend, so people lose track of how much they have spent.","uz":"Raqamli pul sarflash ogʻriqsiz tuyuladi, shuning uchun odamlar qancha sarflaganini hisobdan chiqarib qoʻyadi.","ch":[["lose track of","...ning hisobini yoʻqotmoq"],["feel painless","ogʻriqsiz tuyulmoq"]]},{"c":"18.5","p":true,"en":"Contactless payment reduces physical contact and limits the spread of germs.","uz":"Kontaktsiz toʻlov jismoniy aloqani kamaytiradi va mikroblar tarqalishini cheklaydi.","ch":[["contactless payment","kontaktsiz toʻlov"],["the spread of germs","mikroblar tarqalishi"]]},{"c":"18.6","p":false,"en":"Elderly people who cannot use apps may have to travel long distances to find a cash machine, which is physically tiring.","uz":"Ilovalardan foydalana olmaydigan keksalar bankomat topish uchun uzoq yoʻl yurishi mumkin, bu esa jismonan charchatadi.","ch":[["travel long distances","uzoq masofa bosib oʻtmoq"],["physically tiring","jismonan charchatuvchi"]]},{"c":"18.7","p":true,"en":"Friends can split the bill instantly and send money to relatives with a single tap.","uz":"Doʻstlar hisobni bir zumda boʻlishib, bir bosishda qarindoshlariga pul joʻnatishi mumkin.","ch":[["split the bill","hisobni teng boʻlishmoq"],["send money to relatives","qarindoshlarga pul joʻnatmoq"]]},{"c":"18.8","p":false,"en":"Elderly and rural people who are not tech-savvy may feel excluded from society.","uz":"Texnologiyadan xabardor boʻlmagan keksa va qishloq aholisi jamiyatdan chetlatilgandek his qilishi mumkin.","ch":[["tech-savvy","texnologiyani yaxshi biladigan"],["feel excluded","chetlatilgandek his qilmoq"]]},{"c":"18.9","p":true,"en":"Digital payments cut transaction costs and offer cashback and loyalty rewards.","uz":"Raqamli toʻlovlar tranzaksiya xarajatlarini kamaytiradi va keshbek hamda sodiqlik mukofotlarini taklif qiladi.","ch":[["cut transaction costs","tranzaksiya xarajatlarini kamaytirmoq"],["cashback","keshbek (pulning bir qismini qaytarish)"]]},{"c":"18.10","p":false,"en":"Cybercriminals can steal card details and cause people to become victims of fraud.","uz":"Kiberjinoyatchilar karta ma’lumotlarini oʻgʻirlab, odamlarni firibgarlik qurboniga aylantirishi mumkin.","ch":[["steal card details","karta ma’lumotlarini oʻgʻirlamoq"],["become a victim of fraud","firibgarlik qurboni boʻlmoq"]]}]},{"n":19,"title":"Demanding High-Paying Jobs","uz":"Yuqori maoshli, lekin mashaqqatli ish","q":"Some people choose well-paid jobs with long working hours. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","ideas":[{"c":"19.1","p":true,"en":"Succeeding in a challenging career makes people feel valued and take pride in their career.","uz":"Qiyin kasbda muvaffaqiyatga erishish odamlarni oʻzini qadrlangandek his qilishga va kasbidan faxrlanishga undaydi.","ch":[["feel valued","oʻzini qadrlangandek his qilmoq"],["take pride in one’s career","kasbidan faxrlanmoq"]]},{"c":"19.2","p":false,"en":"Long hours and tight deadlines leave workers emotionally drained.","uz":"Uzoq ish soatlari va siqiq muddatlar ishchilarni ruhan holdan toydiradi.","ch":[["tight deadline","siqiq muddat"],["emotionally drained","ruhan holdan toygan"]]},{"c":"19.3","p":true,"en":"Complex responsibilities sharpen decision-making and stimulate professional growth.","uz":"Murakkab mas’uliyatlar qaror qabul qilishni charxlaydi va kasbiy oʻsishni ragʻbatlantiradi.","ch":[["sharpen decision-making","qaror qabul qilishni charxlamoq"],["professional growth","kasbiy oʻsish"]]},{"c":"19.4","p":false,"en":"Non-stop pressure can lead to burnout and cloud one’s judgement.","uz":"Toʻxtovsiz bosim ruhiy-jismoniy holdan toyishga olib kelishi va mulohazani xiralashtirishi mumkin.","ch":[["lead to burnout","holdan toyishga olib kelmoq"],["cloud one’s judgement","mulohazani xiralashtirmoq"]]},{"c":"19.5","p":true,"en":"High earners can afford gym memberships and regular check-ups.","uz":"Yuqori daromadlilar sport zali a’zoligi va muntazam tibbiy koʻriklarga qodir boʻladi.","ch":[["afford gym memberships","sport zali a’zoligiga qodir boʻlmoq"],["regular check-ups","muntazam tibbiy koʻrik"]]},{"c":"19.6","p":false,"en":"Skipping meals and sleeping little can ruin one’s health over time.","uz":"Ovqatni tashlab ketish va kam uxlash vaqt oʻtishi bilan sogʻliqni buzadi.","ch":[["skip meals","ovqatni tashlab ketmoq"],["ruin one’s health","sogʻliqni buzmoq"]]},{"c":"19.7","p":true,"en":"Professional success earns respect and helps people expand their network.","uz":"Kasbiy muvaffaqiyat hurmat keltiradi va odamlarga aloqalar doirasini kengaytirishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["earn respect","hurmat qozonmoq"],["expand one’s network","aloqalar doirasini kengaytirmoq"]]},{"c":"19.8","p":false,"en":"Workaholics miss out on family time and neglect friendships.","uz":"Ishga berilganlar oila bilan oʻtkaziladigan vaqtdan mahrum boʻladi va doʻstliklarni e’tiborsiz qoldiradi.","ch":[["miss out on family time","oila vaqtidan mahrum boʻlmoq"],["neglect friendships","doʻstliklarni e’tiborsiz qoldirmoq"]]},{"c":"19.9","p":true,"en":"Generous salaries allow workers to buy a home and secure their future.","uz":"Yuqori maosh ishchilarga uy sotib olish va kelajagini ta’minlash imkonini beradi.","ch":[["generous salary","yuqori maosh"],["buy a home","uy sotib olmoq"],["secure one’s future","kelajagini ta’minlamoq"]]},{"c":"19.10","p":false,"en":"Overworked people often spend lavishly to compensate for the time they never have.","uz":"Ish bosimi ostidagilar hech qachon topa olmaydigan vaqti oʻrnini qoplash uchun koʻpincha isrofgarchilik qiladi.","ch":[["spend lavishly","isrofgarchilik qilmoq"],["compensate for","...ning oʻrnini qoplamoq"]]}]},{"n":20,"title":"Volunteering","uz":"Koʻngillilik faoliyati","q":"Some people think everyone should do volunteer work. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","ideas":[{"c":"20.1","p":true,"en":"Helping others gives volunteers a deep sense of fulfilment and boosts their happiness.","uz":"Boshqalarga yordam berish koʻngillilarga chuqur qoniqish hissini beradi va ularning baxtini oshiradi.","ch":[["a deep sense of fulfilment","chuqur qoniqish hissi"],["boost happiness","baxtni oshirmoq"]]},{"c":"20.2","p":false,"en":"Seeing people suffer can be emotionally draining and leave volunteers heartbroken.","uz":"Odamlarning azob chekayotganini koʻrish ruhan toliqtiradi va koʻngillilarni qalbi vayron qiladi.","ch":[["emotionally draining","ruhan toliqtiradigan"],["heartbroken","qalbi sinib, koʻngli vayron boʻlgan"]]},{"c":"20.3","p":true,"en":"Volunteers gain a new perspective and acquire practical skills.","uz":"Koʻngillilar yangi nuqtai nazarga ega boʻladi va amaliy koʻnikmalarni egallaydi.","ch":[["gain a new perspective","yangicha qarashga ega boʻlmoq"],["acquire practical skills","amaliy koʻnikmalarni egallamoq"]]},{"c":"20.4","p":false,"en":"Unpaid tasks beside study or work can leave people overwhelmed as they juggle commitments.","uz":"Oʻqish yoki ishdan tashqari haq toʻlanmaydigan vazifalar odamni charchatadi, chunki ular bir necha majburiyatni birga olib borishga majbur.","ch":[["overwhelmed","boshi qotgan, bosim ostida qolgan"],["juggle commitments","bir necha majburiyatni uddalamoq"]]},{"c":"20.5","p":true,"en":"Active tasks like planting trees keep volunteers fit and give them plenty of fresh air.","uz":"Daraxt ekish kabi faol ishlar koʻngillilarni baquvvat saqlaydi va ularga koʻp toza havo beradi.","ch":[["fit","sogʻlom va baquvvat"],["plenty of fresh air","koʻp toza havo"]]},{"c":"20.6","p":false,"en":"Physically demanding work in poor conditions may cause fatigue and risk injury.","uz":"Yomon sharoitdagi jismonan ogʻir ish charchoqni keltirib chiqarishi va jarohat xavfini tugʻdirishi mumkin.","ch":[["physically demanding","jismonan ogʻir"],["risk injury","jarohat xavfini tugʻdirmoq"]]},{"c":"20.7","p":true,"en":"Volunteering brings communities together and helps people make like-minded friends.","uz":"Koʻngillilik jamoalarni birlashtiradi va odamlarga fikrdosh doʻstlar orttirishga yordam beradi.","ch":[["bring communities together","jamoalarni birlashtirmoq"],["make like-minded friends","fikrdosh doʻstlar orttirmoq"]]},{"c":"20.8","p":false,"en":"Volunteers may spend less time with family and friends, which can cause tension at home.","uz":"Koʻngillilar oila va doʻstlariga kamroq vaqt ajratishi mumkin, bu esa uyda tarangliklarni keltirib chiqaradi.","ch":[["spend less time with","...bilan kamroq vaqt oʻtkazmoq"],["cause tension","taranglik keltirib chiqarmoq"]]},{"c":"20.9","p":true,"en":"Volunteer experience strengthens a CV and improves job prospects.","uz":"Koʻngillilik tajribasi rezyumeni boyitadi va ish topish imkoniyatlarini yaxshilaydi.","ch":[["strengthen a CV","rezyumeni mustahkamlamoq"],["improve job prospects","ish topish imkoniyatini yaxshilamoq"]]},{"c":"20.10","p":false,"en":"Working unpaid means giving up earnings, and volunteers often pay out of their own pocket for travel and food.","uz":"Haq toʻlanmaydigan ish daromaddan voz kechishni anglatadi, koʻngillilar esa yoʻlkira va ovqat uchun koʻpincha oʻz choʻntagidan toʻlaydi.","ch":[["pay out of one’s own pocket","oʻz choʻntagidan toʻlamoq"],["travel and food costs","yoʻlkira va ovqat xarajatlari"]]}]}]},W=[{"n":1,"q":"Some people say a vegetarian diet is better for health. Do you agree?","kind":"Agree / disagree","title":"Vegetarian diet","essay":["The question of whether a vegetarian diet is healthier than one that includes meat has been widely discussed in recent years. While meat provides some essential nutrients, I believe that a well-planned vegetarian diet is better for long-term health.","There are several reasons why critics doubt vegetarian diets, one of which is that meat provides «essential nutrients». Because beef and fish are rich in protein and vitamin B12, people who give up meat may «feel tired and weak». This can lead to nutritional deficiencies, thereby weakening the immune system. For example, a teenager who never eats meat or takes supplements may often fall ill.","However, I am convinced that a vegetarian diet is healthier, mainly because it lowers the «risk of heart disease». When people «replace red meat with» beans, vegetables and whole grains, they «take in less saturated fat», which leads to healthier blood pressure and cholesterol levels. As a result, they are less likely to «suffer from serious illnesses» later in life. Fibre also helps them «maintain a healthy weight». For instance, a man who swaps burgers for lentil soup several times a week may avoid heart problems in his fifties.","In conclusion, although vegetarians must plan their meals carefully, I firmly believe that «a well-balanced diet» without meat is better for health because it protects the heart and supports a healthy weight."],"chunks":[["a lower risk of heart disease","yurak kasalligi xavfi pastroq bo‘lishi"],["replace red meat with","qizil go‘shtni … bilan almashtirmoq"],["take in less saturated fat","kamroq to‘yingan yog‘ iste’mol qilmoq"],["blood pressure","qon bosimi"],["cholesterol levels","xolesterin darajasi"],["suffer from serious illnesses","og‘ir kasalliklardan aziyat chekmoq"],["maintain a healthy weight","sog‘lom vaznni saqlamoq"],["rich in fibre","tolaga boy"],["keep people full for longer","odamni uzoqroq to‘q tutmoq"],["reduce the desire to snack","tishlab olish istagini kamaytirmoq"],["sugary food","qandli (shirin) ovqat"],["control one’s weight","vaznini nazorat qilmoq"],["strict dieting","qattiq parhez"],["a well-balanced diet","muvozanatli ovqatlanish"],["a plant-based diet","o‘simlik asosidagi parhez"],["essential nutrients","zarur oziq moddalar"],["protein and vitamin B12","oqsil va B12 vitamini"],["feel tired and weak","o‘zini charchagan va holsiz his qilmoq"],["plan one’s meals carefully","ovqatlanishni ehtiyotkorlik bilan rejalashtirmoq"],["processed meat","qayta ishlangan go‘sht"],["boost the immune system","immunitetni mustahkamlamoq"],["improve digestion","hazmni yaxshilamoq"],["whole grains","to‘liq donli mahsulotlar"],["beans and lentils","loviya va yasmiq"],["give up meat","go‘shtni tark etmoq"],["a balanced lifestyle","muvozanatli turmush tarzi"],["nutritional deficiencies","oziq moddalar yetishmovchiligi"],["take supplements","vitamin qo‘shimchalarini qabul qilmoq"],["long-term health","uzoq muddatli salomatlik"],["protect the heart","yurakni asramoq"]],"wc":225},{"n":2,"q":"What problems can plastic pollution cause, and how can it be solved?","kind":"Problem / solution","title":"Plastic pollution","essay":["Nowadays, plastic waste has become one of the most urgent environmental issues, because it takes hundreds of years to break down. While plastic makes modern life convenient, I believe that its serious damage to nature can be reduced through stricter laws and better education.","There are several serious problems caused by plastic pollution, one of which is the damage it does to «marine life». When plastic bags and bottles «end up in rivers and seas», fish and turtles often «mistake plastic for food», which leads to injury and death. As a result, entire ecosystems are disturbed, thereby threatening the fishing industry. For example, a turtle that swallows a plastic bag may starve because its stomach is blocked.","To solve this problem, governments should «introduce strict rules» on «single-use plastic». By «charging customers for plastic bags» and banning disposable cups, authorities can encourage people to bring «reusable bags» and bottles. This reduces the amount of waste that reaches landfills and oceans. In addition, schools can «raise awareness» among children. For instance, a pupil who learns about recycling may persuade her family to «separate rubbish» at home.","In conclusion, although plastic pollution harms wildlife and the environment, I firmly believe that stricter laws and better education can reduce it significantly."],"chunks":[["single-use plastic","bir martalik plastik"],["marine life","dengiz hayoti"],["end up in rivers and seas","daryo va dengizlarga borib tushmoq"],["mistake plastic for food","plastikni ovqat deb adashmoq"],["disturb ecosystems","ekotizimlarni buzmoq"],["threaten the fishing industry","baliqchilik sohasiga tahdid solmoq"],["swallow a plastic bag","plastik paketni yutib yubormoq"],["break down","parchalanmoq"],["take hundreds of years to decompose","chirishi yuzlab yil talab qilmoq"],["landfill sites","chiqindixonalar"],["introduce strict rules","qat’iy qoidalar joriy etmoq"],["ban disposable cups","bir martalik stakanlarni taqiqlamoq"],["charge customers for plastic bags","xaridorlardan paketlar uchun haq olmoq"],["reusable bags","qayta ishlatiladigan sumkalar"],["raise awareness","xabardorlikni oshirmoq"],["separate rubbish","chiqindilarni ajratmoq"],["recycle waste","chiqindilarni qayta ishlamoq"],["harm wildlife","yovvoyi tabiatga zarar yetkazmoq"],["contaminate soil and water","tuproq va suvni ifloslantirmoq"],["enter the food chain","oziq zanjiriga kirmoq"],["microplastics","mikroplastiklar"],["health risks","sog‘liq uchun xavflar"],["clean up beaches","plyajlarni tozalamoq"],["eco-friendly alternatives","ekologik toza muqobillar"],["biodegradable packaging","biologik parchalanuvchi qadoq"],["impose fines","jarima solmoq"],["tackle the problem","muammoni hal etmoq"],["reduce plastic waste","plastik chiqindilarni kamaytirmoq"],["a throwaway culture","“ishlat-tashla” madaniyati"],["plastic pollution","plastik ifloslanish"]],"wc":208},{"n":3,"q":"Should school students wear uniforms?","kind":"Opinion","title":"School uniforms","essay":["The question of whether school students should wear uniforms is widely debated. While uniforms may limit self-expression, I believe that they are beneficial because they create equality and save money.","There are several reasons why critics dislike uniforms, one of which is that they «restrict individuality». When every pupil wears the same clothes, teenagers may feel unable to «express their personality» and creativity. This can lead to frustration, thereby «reducing enthusiasm for school». For example, a girl who loves fashion may feel bored by wearing the same grey skirt every day.","However, I am convinced that uniforms are beneficial, mainly because they «promote equality» among students. By removing the «pressure to wear expensive brands», schools prevent children from comparing their families’ incomes. As a result, pupils feel more equal and «bullying» about clothes becomes less likely. Uniforms also «save parents money», because they do not need to buy «a large wardrobe». For instance, a family with three children may spend far less when each child needs only two uniforms.","In conclusion, although uniforms may limit self-expression, I firmly believe that they create «a fairer learning environment», and I therefore think schools should keep them."],"chunks":[["wear a school uniform","maktab formasini kiymoq"],["restrict individuality","individuallikni cheklamoq"],["express one’s personality","shaxsiyatini ifodalamoq"],["reduce enthusiasm for school","maktabga bo‘lgan ishtiyoqni pasaytirmoq"],["feel frustrated","g‘ashi kelmoq, xafa bo‘lmoq"],["promote equality","tenglikni targ‘ib qilmoq"],["pressure to wear expensive brands","qimmat brendlarni kiyish bosimi"],["compare family incomes","oilalar daromadini solishtirmoq"],["bullying","bezorilik, bulling"],["peer pressure","tengdoshlar bosimi"],["save parents money","ota-onalarning pulini tejamoq"],["a large wardrobe","katta kiyim-kechak to‘plami"],["a sense of belonging","o‘zini jamoaning bir qismi his qilish"],["school spirit","maktab ruhi"],["build a sense of community","jamoa tuyg‘usini shakllantirmoq"],["focus on studies","o‘qishga e’tibor qaratmoq"],["avoid distractions","chalg‘ituvchi narsalardan qochmoq"],["a strict dress code","qat’iy kiyinish qoidalari"],["look smart and professional","ozoda va professional ko‘rinmoq"],["make students easy to identify","o‘quvchilarni tanib olishni osonlashtirmoq"],["uncomfortable fabric","noqulay mato"],["daily routine","kundalik tartib"],["get dressed quickly","tez kiyinib olmoq"],["improve discipline","intizomni yaxshilamoq"],["a fairer learning environment","adolatliroq ta’lim muhiti"],["wear the same clothes","bir xil kiyim kiymoq"],["express creativity","ijodkorlikni ifodalamoq"],["follow fashion trends","moda tendensiyalariga ergashmoq"],["cost-effective","tejamkor"],["limit self-expression","o‘zini ifoda etishni cheklamoq"]],"wc":194},{"n":4,"q":"Is it better to shop online or in physical stores?","kind":"Opinion / comparison","title":"Online vs physical shopping","essay":["In recent times, shopping habits have changed dramatically as more people buy goods online. While physical stores still have some advantages, I believe that online shopping is the better option for most people.","There are several benefits of traditional shopping, one of which is that customers can «examine products before buying» them. When shoppers touch fabrics or «try on shoes», they can be sure about quality and size. This helps them avoid disappointment, thereby reducing the number of «returned goods». For example, a man who buys a coat in a shop can check immediately whether it «fits properly».","However, I believe that online shopping is better, mainly because it «saves a great deal of time». By ordering from home, people no longer need to travel to «crowded shopping malls» or «queue at the checkout». As a result, they can use these hours for work, study or relaxation. Online shops also offer lower prices because they have «lower running costs». For instance, a busy mother can «compare prices» on her phone while cooking dinner and still receive the goods the next day.","In conclusion, although physical stores allow customers to check items, I firmly believe that online shopping is superior because it is faster, cheaper and more convenient."],"chunks":[["shopping habits","xarid qilish odatlari"],["examine products before buying","sotib olishdan oldin mahsulotni sinchiklab ko‘rmoq"],["try on shoes","poyabzalni kiyib ko‘rmoq"],["be sure about quality","sifatiga ishonch hosil qilmoq"],["avoid disappointment","hafsalasi pir bo‘lishidan qochmoq"],["returned goods","qaytarilgan tovarlar"],["fit properly","(o‘lcham jihatidan) to‘g‘ri kelmoq"],["save a great deal of time","ko‘p vaqtni tejamoq"],["crowded shopping malls","gavjum savdo markazlari"],["queue at the checkout","kassada navbatda turmoq"],["place an order online","onlayn buyurtma bermoq"],["free delivery","bepul yetkazib berish"],["next-day delivery","ertasi kuni yetkazib berish"],["compare prices","narxlarni solishtirmoq"],["lower running costs","pastroq operatsion xarajatlar"],["offer discounts","chegirmalar taklif qilmoq"],["a wide range of products","mahsulotlarning keng assortimenti"],["at the click of a button","bir tugma bosish bilan"],["from the comfort of one’s home","uyda, qulay o‘tirgan holda"],["impulse buying","o‘ylamay xarid qilish"],["overspend","ortiqcha pul sarflamoq"],["receive a refund","pulni qaytarib olmoq"],["read customer reviews","mijozlar sharhlarini o‘qimoq"],["secure payment","xavfsiz to‘lov"],["poor-quality goods","sifatsiz tovarlar"],["support local shops","mahalliy do‘konlarni qo‘llab-quvvatlamoq"],["face-to-face advice","yuzma-yuz maslahat"],["helpful shop assistants","yordam beradigan sotuvchilar"],["a busy schedule","band jadval"],["the shopping experience","xarid qilish tajribasi"]],"wc":207},{"n":5,"q":"Some people believe social media has a positive influence on young people, while others argue it does more harm than good. What is your opinion?","kind":"Discuss both views + opinion","title":"Social media and young people","essay":["Nowadays, social media plays a central role in the lives of young people. While it connects them and teaches useful skills, I believe that it does more harm than good.","There are several advantages of social media for teenagers, one of which is that it helps them «pick up new skills». When young people watch «free video tutorials», they can study languages, music or coding without paying for lessons. This often leads to greater confidence, thereby «opening doors to future careers». For example, a teenager who learns video editing online may later «start a small business».","However, I am convinced that social media does more harm, mainly because it «damages mental health». By constantly «comparing themselves with influencers», teenagers begin to «feel inadequate» about their appearance and lives. As a result, they may suffer from anxiety and «low self-esteem», which affects their studies and friendships. «Endless scrolling» also «shortens attention span». For instance, a student who checks notifications every few minutes may fail to finish his homework.","In conclusion, although social media offers learning opportunities, I firmly believe that its negative effects on mental health outweigh them, and I therefore think parents should «limit screen time»."],"chunks":[["the younger generation","yosh avlod"],["connect people","odamlarni bog‘lamoq"],["pick up new skills","yangi ko‘nikmalarni o‘rganib olmoq"],["free video tutorials","bepul video darsliklar"],["gain confidence","ishonch orttirmoq"],["open doors to future careers","kelajak kasblari uchun eshiklarni ochmoq"],["start a small business","kichik biznes boshlamoq"],["damage mental health","ruhiy salomatlikka zarar yetkazmoq"],["compare oneself with influencers","o‘zini bloggerlar bilan solishtirmoq"],["feel inadequate","o‘zini yetarli emasdek his qilmoq"],["suffer from anxiety","xavotirdan aziyat chekmoq"],["low self-esteem","o‘zini past baholash"],["endless scrolling","cheksiz skroll qilish"],["shorten attention span","diqqat davomiyligini qisqartirmoq"],["check notifications","bildirishnomalarni tekshirmoq"],["fail to finish homework","uy vazifasini tugata olmaslik"],["cyberbullying","kiberbezorilik"],["spread misinformation","noto‘g‘ri ma’lumot tarqatmoq"],["become addicted to","…ga qaram bo‘lib qolmoq"],["waste time","vaqtni behuda sarflamoq"],["disrupted sleep patterns","buzilgan uyqu tartibi"],["a sedentary lifestyle","kam harakatli turmush tarzi"],["stay in touch with friends","do‘stlar bilan aloqada bo‘lmoq"],["share common interests","umumiy qiziqishlarni bo‘lishmoq"],["build an online community","onlayn jamoa qurmoq"],["limit screen time","ekran vaqtini cheklamoq"],["set clear boundaries","aniq chegaralar belgilamoq"],["peer approval","tengdoshlar tasdig‘i"],["a polished online image","sayqallangan onlayn qiyofa"],["have a lasting effect on","…ga uzoq muddatli ta’sir ko‘rsatmoq"]],"wc":196},{"n":6,"q":"Some people believe modern technology makes us more connected than ever, while others argue that it is causing people to become more isolated. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Technology: connected or isolated?","essay":["In recent times, modern technology has changed the way people communicate. While some argue that it isolates people, I believe that technology makes us more connected than ever.","There are several reasons why critics worry about technology, one of which is that it «reduces face-to-face contact». When family members sit together but «stare at their screens», they rarely have real conversations. This often leads to loneliness, thereby weakening «close relationships». For example, a teenager who chats with friends online all evening may stop visiting them in person.","However, I am convinced that technology connects people, mainly because it allows them to «stay in touch» across long distances. By using video calls and messaging apps, relatives who live in different countries can share daily news at no cost. As a result, they feel closer and more supported, which improves their well-being. For instance, a student living abroad can talk to her parents every evening and still feel part of the family.","In conclusion, although technology may reduce personal contact, I firmly believe that it makes us more connected because it removes distance and brings people together."],"chunks":[["reduce face-to-face contact","yuzma-yuz muloqotni kamaytirmoq"],["stare at one’s screen","ekranga tikilib o‘tirmoq"],["have real conversations","haqiqiy suhbatlar qurmoq"],["weaken close relationships","yaqin munosabatlarni zaiflashtirmoq"],["feel isolated","o‘zini ajralgan his qilmoq"],["drift apart","bir-biridan uzoqlashmoq"],["stay in touch","aloqada bo‘lib turmoq"],["across long distances","uzoq masofalarga qaramay"],["video calls","video qo‘ng‘iroqlar"],["messaging apps","xabar almashish ilovalari"],["at no cost","bepul"],["share daily news","kundalik yangiliklarni ulashmoq"],["build online communities","onlayn jamoalar qurmoq"],["share common interests","umumiy qiziqishlarni bo‘lishmoq"],["overcome distance","masofani yengmoq"],["a sense of loneliness","yolg‘izlik hissi"],["virtual friendships","virtual do‘stliklar"],["real-life interaction","real hayotdagi muloqot"],["depend on technology","texnologiyaga qaram bo‘lmoq"],["bring people closer","odamlarni yaqinlashtirmoq"],["connect with others","boshqalar bilan bog‘lanmoq"],["superficial relationships","yuzaki munosabatlar"],["develop social skills","ijtimoiy ko‘nikmalarni rivojlantirmoq"],["spend quality time","sifatli vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["instant communication","bir zumda aloqa"],["make new friends","yangi do‘stlar orttirmoq"],["lose touch with","bilan aloqani yo‘qotmoq"],["a global network","global tarmoq"],["emotional support","hissiy qo‘llab-quvvatlash"],["feel part of the family","o‘zini oilaning bir qismi his qilmoq"]],"wc":185},{"n":7,"q":"Some people believe that mobile phone use during lessons should be banned in schools. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Phones in lessons","essay":["The question of whether mobile phones should be allowed in lessons has become a hot topic in schools. While phones can be useful learning tools, I believe that their use during lessons should be banned.","There are several reasons why some teachers allow phones, one of which is that they can be «useful learning tools». When pupils use dictionary apps or educational websites, they can «look up information» quickly and learn at their own pace. This often makes lessons more interactive, thereby increasing motivation. For example, a student who finds the meaning of a new word on his phone can continue the discussion immediately.","However, I am convinced that phones should be banned during lessons, mainly because they «distract students from learning». By checking messages and social media, pupils «lose concentration» and miss important explanations. As a result, their grades may fall, which worries teachers and parents. Phones also encourage «cheating in exams». For instance, a student who secretly searches for answers under the desk gains an unfair advantage over honest classmates.","In conclusion, although phones can support learning, I firmly believe that they should be banned in classrooms because they harm concentration and fairness."],"chunks":[["a useful learning tool","foydali o‘quv vositasi"],["look up information","ma’lumot qidirib topmoq"],["dictionary apps","lug‘at ilovalari"],["learn at one’s own pace","o‘z sur’atida o‘rganmoq"],["make lessons more interactive","darslarni interaktivroq qilmoq"],["increase motivation","motivatsiyani oshirmoq"],["distract students from learning","o‘quvchilarni o‘qishdan chalg‘itmoq"],["lose concentration","diqqatni yo‘qotmoq"],["miss important explanations","muhim tushuntirishlarni o‘tkazib yubormoq"],["check messages","xabarlarni tekshirmoq"],["grades may fall","baholar tushib ketishi mumkin"],["cheat in exams","imtihonda ko‘chirmoq"],["gain an unfair advantage","nohaq ustunlikka erishmoq"],["honest classmates","halol sinfdoshlar"],["enforce a ban","taqiqni amalda qo‘llamoq"],["a strict school policy","maktabning qat’iy siyosati"],["pay attention in class","darsda diqqatli bo‘lmoq"],["face-to-face discussion","yuzma-yuz muhokama"],["disrupt the lesson","darsni buzmoq"],["become addicted to phones","telefonga qaram bo‘lib qolmoq"],["waste valuable time","qimmatli vaqtni yo‘qotmoq"],["cause cyberbullying","kiberbezorilikni keltirib chiqarmoq"],["concentrate on the task","topshiriqqa e’tibor qaratmoq"],["improve academic performance","o‘zlashtirishni yaxshilamoq"],["use phones responsibly","telefondan mas’uliyat bilan foydalanmoq"],["emergency contact","favqulodda aloqa"],["a distraction-free environment","chalg‘ituvchilarsiz muhit"],["teach self-discipline","o‘zini tutishni o‘rgatmoq"],["social media notifications","ijtimoiy tarmoq bildirishnomalari"],["unfair advantage","nohaq ustunlik"]],"wc":195},{"n":8,"q":"Families spend less time together than they used to in the past. What are the advantages and disadvantages of this trend?","kind":"Advantages / disadvantages","title":"Families spend less time together","essay":["Nowadays, many families spend less time together than they did in the past. While this trend gives family members more independence, I believe that its disadvantages are more serious.","There are several advantages of this trend, one of which is that family members gain «greater independence». When parents and children pursue their own careers and hobbies, they develop new skills and «broaden their horizons». This often leads to higher confidence, thereby improving their «quality of life». For example, a teenager who joins a sports club after school may become more disciplined and sociable.","However, I believe that the disadvantages are more serious, mainly because less time together «weakens family bonds». By eating separately and «spending hours on their phones», relatives rarely share their problems or feelings. As a result, children may feel unsupported, which can lead to stress and poor behaviour. For instance, a girl who never talks to her parents about school may hide her difficulties until they become serious.","In conclusion, although independence has some benefits, I firmly believe that the disadvantages of spending less time together outweigh them, and families should make time for each other."],"chunks":[["greater independence","ko‘proq mustaqillik"],["pursue a career","karyera qilmoq"],["broaden one’s horizons","dunyoqarashini kengaytirmoq"],["improve the quality of life","hayot sifatini yaxshilamoq"],["develop new skills","yangi ko‘nikmalarni rivojlantirmoq"],["become more disciplined","intizomliroq bo‘lmoq"],["join a sports club","sport klubiga a’zo bo‘lmoq"],["weaken family bonds","oilaviy rishtalarni zaiflashtirmoq"],["spend hours on phones","soatlab telefonda vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["eat separately","alohida ovqatlanmoq"],["share problems and feelings","muammo va his-tuyg‘ularni ulashmoq"],["feel unsupported","o‘zini qo‘llab-quvvatlanmagandek his qilmoq"],["hide one’s difficulties","qiyinchiliklarini yashirmoq"],["poor behaviour","yomon xulq"],["a busy lifestyle","band turmush tarzi"],["long working hours","uzoq ish soatlari"],["demanding careers","talabchan kasblar"],["spend quality time together","birga sifatli vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["have a family meal","oilaviy ovqatlanmoq"],["communication breaks down","muloqot buziladi"],["generation gap","avlodlar o‘rtasidagi tafovut"],["emotional support","hissiy qo‘llab-quvvatlash"],["close-knit family","o‘zaro yaqin oila"],["strengthen relationships","munosabatlarni mustahkamlamoq"],["lead to stress","stressga olib kelmoq"],["feel lonely at home","uyda o‘zini yolg‘iz his qilmoq"],["make time for each other","bir-biri uchun vaqt ajratmoq"],["family traditions","oilaviy an’analar"],["set a good example","yaxshi namuna bo‘lmoq"],["a sense of security","xavfsizlik hissi"]],"wc":189},{"n":9,"q":"Some people think young people should spend their free time in youth centres, while others believe they should spend it at home with their families. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Youth centres or family time","essay":["In recent times, there has been a debate about where young people should spend their free time. While youth centres offer useful activities, I believe that time at home with the family is more valuable.","There are several reasons why people support youth centres, one of which is that they offer «organised activities». When teenagers join sports clubs or art classes, they «make new friends» and develop useful skills. This often keeps them away from «bad influences», thereby protecting their future. For example, a boy who plays football at a youth centre may learn teamwork and discipline.","However, I am convinced that spending free time with the family is more valuable, mainly because it «strengthens family bonds». By eating, talking and relaxing together, young people feel loved and understood. As a result, they are more likely to share their problems and follow good advice. Family time is also free. For instance, a girl who cooks dinner with her mother learns practical skills and enjoys a close relationship.","In conclusion, although youth centres offer useful activities, I firmly believe that young people should spend more of their free time at home with their families."],"chunks":[["organised activities","tashkil etilgan mashg‘ulotlar"],["make new friends","yangi do‘stlar orttirmoq"],["develop useful skills","foydali ko‘nikmalarni rivojlantirmoq"],["keep away from bad influences","yomon ta’sirdan uzoq tutmoq"],["learn teamwork","jamoa bo‘lib ishlashni o‘rganmoq"],["learn discipline","intizomni o‘rganmoq"],["a safe environment","xavfsiz muhit"],["professional supervision","professional nazorat"],["strengthen family bonds","oilaviy rishtalarni mustahkamlamoq"],["feel loved and understood","o‘zini sevilgan va tushunilgan his qilmoq"],["share problems","muammolarni ulashmoq"],["follow good advice","yaxshi maslahatga amal qilmoq"],["cook dinner together","birga kechki ovqat tayyorlamoq"],["learn practical skills","amaliy ko‘nikmalarni o‘rganmoq"],["a close relationship","yaqin munosabat"],["spend time at home","uyda vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["free of charge","bepul"],["membership fees","a’zolik to‘lovlari"],["peer pressure","tengdoshlar bosimi"],["socialise with peers","tengdoshlar bilan muloqot qilmoq"],["build confidence","ishonchni shakllantirmoq"],["take up a hobby","hobbi bilan shug‘ullanmoq"],["show respect for elders","kattalarni hurmat qilmoq"],["pass on family values","oilaviy qadriyatlarni avlodga o‘tkazmoq"],["a sense of belonging","jamoaga tegishlilik hissi"],["become independent","mustaqil bo‘lmoq"],["get into trouble","muammoga duch kelmoq"],["supervised by adults","kattalar nazorati ostida"],["enjoy a healthy lifestyle","sog‘lom turmush tarzidan bahramand bo‘lmoq"],["balance free time","bo‘sh vaqtni muvozanatlamoq"]],"wc":193},{"n":10,"q":"Some people say that eating out in cafes and restaurants is better than cooking at home. Do you agree?","kind":"Agree / disagree","title":"Eating out vs cooking at home","essay":["The question of whether eating out is better than cooking at home is often discussed. While restaurants are convenient, I believe that cooking at home is healthier and cheaper.","There are several reasons why people enjoy eating out, one of which is that it is «convenient and time-saving». When workers come home exhausted, they do not have to shop, cook or «wash the dishes». This often leaves more time for relaxing, thereby reducing stress. For example, a busy nurse who finishes work at nine may prefer a quick dinner in a café.","However, I believe that cooking at home is better, mainly because it is «much healthier». By preparing their own meals, people can choose «fresh ingredients» and control the amount of salt, sugar and oil. As a result, they avoid weight problems, which improves their long-term health. Home cooking also saves money. For instance, a family of four that eats out three times a week may spend several hundred dollars a month, whereas cooking at home costs far less.","In conclusion, although eating out is convenient, I firmly believe that cooking at home is the better option because it is healthier and cheaper."],"chunks":[["eat out","restoranda/kafede ovqatlanmoq"],["convenient and time-saving","qulay va vaqtni tejaydigan"],["come home exhausted","uyga horib-charchab kelmoq"],["wash the dishes","idish yuvmoq"],["leave more time for relaxing","dam olishga ko‘proq vaqt qoldirmoq"],["reduce stress","stressni kamaytirmoq"],["a quick dinner","tez kechki ovqat"],["prepare one’s own meals","ovqatni o‘zi tayyorlamoq"],["choose fresh ingredients","yangi masalliqlarni tanlamoq"],["control the amount of salt and sugar","tuz va shakar miqdorini nazorat qilmoq"],["avoid weight problems","ortiqcha vazn muammosidan qochmoq"],["improve long-term health","uzoq muddatli salomatlikni yaxshilamoq"],["save money","pulni tejamoq"],["home-cooked meals","uyda pishirilgan ovqatlar"],["processed food","qayta ishlangan oziq-ovqat"],["unhealthy fast food","nosog‘lom tezkor ovqat"],["a wide choice of dishes","taomlarning keng tanlovi"],["try new cuisines","yangi oshxonalarni tatib ko‘rmoq"],["socialise with friends","do‘stlar bilan ko‘rishmoq"],["a relaxed atmosphere","erkin muhit"],["bring the family together","oilani jamlamoq"],["learn to cook","ovqat pishirishni o‘rganmoq"],["do the grocery shopping","oziq-ovqat xaridini qilmoq"],["eat balanced meals","muvozanatli ovqatlanmoq"],["cost a fortune","juda qimmatga tushmoq"],["service charge","xizmat haqi"],["portion size","porsiya hajmi"],["a sense of achievement","muvaffaqiyat hissi"],["special occasions","alohida (bayram) holatlar"],["save time on cooking","pishirishda vaqtni tejamoq"]],"wc":194},{"n":11,"q":"Some people believe travelling in a group is better than travelling alone. What are the advantages and disadvantages?","kind":"Advantages / disadvantages","title":"Group travel vs travelling alone","essay":["Nowadays, tourists can choose between joining a group and travelling alone. While group travel is safe and convenient, I believe that travelling alone has more advantages.","There are several benefits of group travel, one of which is that it is «safer and less stressful». When tourists travel with a guide, they do not worry about «getting lost» or booking hotels. This allows them to relax, thereby enjoying the trip more. For example, an elderly couple visiting a foreign country may feel more confident on an organised tour.","However, I believe that travelling alone has more advantages, mainly because it gives people «complete freedom». By choosing their own routes and schedule, solo travellers can spend more time at the places they love. As a result, they often have more memorable experiences, which improves their independence. Group tours also have a fixed programme. For instance, a traveller who loves museums can stay all day, whereas a group may leave after one hour.","In conclusion, although group travel is safe and convenient, I firmly believe that the freedom of travelling alone makes it the better choice for many people."],"chunks":[["travel in a group","guruh bo‘lib sayohat qilmoq"],["travel alone","yolg‘iz sayohat qilmoq"],["safer and less stressful","xavfsizroq va kamroq stressli"],["travel with a guide","gid bilan sayohat qilmoq"],["get lost","yo‘lini yo‘qotmoq"],["book hotels","mehmonxonalarni band qilmoq"],["an organised tour","tashkil etilgan tur"],["feel more confident","o‘zini ishonchliroq his qilmoq"],["complete freedom","to‘liq erkinlik"],["choose one’s own route","o‘z marshrutini tanlamoq"],["a flexible schedule","moslashuvchan jadval"],["a fixed programme","qat’iy dastur"],["memorable experiences","unutilmas tajribalar"],["make lifelong friends","umrbod do‘stlar orttirmoq"],["share the costs","xarajatlarni bo‘lishmoq"],["split the bill","hisobni bo‘lishmoq"],["cut costs","xarajatlarni qisqartirmoq"],["a language barrier","til to‘sig‘i"],["meet local people","mahalliy aholi bilan tanishmoq"],["step out of one’s comfort zone","o‘z qulaylik doirasidan chiqmoq"],["gain independence","mustaqillikka erishmoq"],["have disagreements","kelishmovchiliklarga ega bo‘lmoq"],["follow the crowd","olomonga ergashmoq"],["spend more time at places","joylarda ko‘proq vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["a solo traveller","yolg‘iz sayohatchi"],["tourist attractions","turistik diqqatga sazovor joylar"],["travel on a budget","tejamkor sayohat qilmoq"],["have a sense of adventure","sarguzasht ruhiga ega bo‘lmoq"],["discover hidden places","yashirin joylarni kashf etmoq"],["reduce the risk","xavfni kamaytirmoq"]],"wc":186},{"n":12,"q":"Some people think sports facilities should be free for everyone. Do you agree?","kind":"Agree / disagree","title":"Free sports facilities","essay":["In recent times, rising obesity levels have led to discussions about public sports facilities. While free facilities are expensive to maintain, I believe that they should be free for everyone.","There are several reasons why some people oppose free facilities, one of which is that they are «expensive to maintain». Because swimming pools and stadiums need cleaning, repairs and staff, governments may struggle to cover the «running costs». This can lead to poor quality, thereby disappointing users. For example, a free gym without enough equipment may become overcrowded and unsafe.","However, I am convinced that sports facilities should be free, mainly because they «improve public health». By removing the cost, authorities encourage people of all ages to «exercise regularly». As a result, fewer citizens suffer from obesity and heart disease, which reduces the pressure on hospitals. Free access also gives low-income families equal chances. For instance, a boy from a poor family can join a football team without asking his parents for money.","In conclusion, although free facilities are costly, I firmly believe that governments should provide them because they improve public health and create equal opportunities."],"chunks":[["free of charge","bepul"],["expensive to maintain","saqlash qimmat"],["running costs","joriy xarajatlar"],["cover the costs","xarajatlarni qoplamoq"],["struggle to afford","ko‘tara olmay qiynalmoq"],["become overcrowded","haddan tashqari gavjum bo‘lmoq"],["poor quality","past sifat"],["a lack of equipment","jihozlar yetishmasligi"],["improve public health","aholi salomatligini yaxshilamoq"],["exercise regularly","muntazam mashq qilmoq"],["suffer from obesity","semizlikdan aziyat chekmoq"],["reduce pressure on hospitals","kasalxonalarga tushadigan yukni kamaytirmoq"],["heart disease","yurak kasalligi"],["low-income families","daromadi past oilalar"],["equal opportunities","teng imkoniyatlar"],["join a football team","futbol jamoasiga qo‘shilmoq"],["encourage an active lifestyle","faol turmush tarzini rag‘batlantirmoq"],["a sedentary lifestyle","kam harakatli turmush tarzi"],["public funds","davlat mablag‘lari"],["taxpayers’ money","soliq to‘lovchilar puli"],["invest in sport","sportga sarmoya kiritmoq"],["build a stadium","stadion qurmoq"],["keep fit","baquvvat saqlamoq"],["reduce healthcare costs","sog‘liqni saqlash xarajatlarini kamaytirmoq"],["talented athletes","iqtidorli sportchilar"],["discover young talent","yosh iste’dodlarni kashf etmoq"],["strengthen community spirit","jamoa ruhini mustahkamlamoq"],["entrance fee","kirish to‘lovi"],["membership fee","a’zolik to‘lovi"],["a healthy generation","sog‘lom avlod"]],"wc":187},{"n":13,"q":"Some people believe libraries are no longer necessary because of the internet. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Libraries and the internet","essay":["The question of whether libraries are still necessary in the age of the internet is often raised. While information is now available online, I believe that libraries remain essential.","There are several reasons why people consider libraries unnecessary, one of which is that information is now «available online». By using search engines and e-books, students can find articles in seconds without leaving home. This saves time, thereby making research easier. For example, a student writing an essay at midnight can read journals online when the library is closed.","However, I am convinced that libraries are still necessary, mainly because they provide «free access to reliable sources». Many academic books and journals are expensive, so people with low incomes cannot afford them. As a result, libraries give everyone equal chances to learn. They also offer «a quiet study environment». For instance, a pupil who lives in a noisy flat can concentrate on homework at a library desk.","In conclusion, although the internet offers fast information, I firmly believe that libraries remain essential because they provide reliable resources and a peaceful place to study."],"chunks":[["available online","onlayn mavjud"],["search engines","qidiruv tizimlari"],["e-books","elektron kitoblar"],["find information in seconds","soniyalarda ma’lumot topmoq"],["save time","vaqtni tejamoq"],["make research easier","tadqiqotni osonlashtirmoq"],["read journals online","jurnallarni onlayn o‘qimoq"],["free access","bepul kirish imkoni"],["reliable sources","ishonchli manbalar"],["unreliable information","ishonchsiz ma’lumot"],["fake news","soxta xabarlar"],["academic books","ilmiy kitoblar"],["cannot afford","(narxini) ko‘tara olmaslik"],["equal chances to learn","o‘qish uchun teng imkoniyatlar"],["a quiet study environment","jim o‘qish muhiti"],["concentrate on homework","uy vazifasiga e’tibor qaratmoq"],["a noisy flat","shovqinli kvartira"],["borrow books","kitob olib turmoq"],["rare books","noyob kitoblar"],["a wide range of resources","resurslarning keng tanlovi"],["librarians’ guidance","kutubxonachilar yo‘l-yo‘rig‘i"],["community hub","jamoat markazi"],["hold events","tadbirlar o‘tkazmoq"],["encourage reading habits","o‘qish odatini rag‘batlantirmoq"],["digital divide","raqamli tengsizlik"],["have no internet access","internetga ulanish imkoniga ega bo‘lmaslik"],["distractions online","onlayn chalg‘ituvchilar"],["spend hours browsing","soatlab internetda kezmoq"],["preserve knowledge","bilimlarni saqlab qolmoq"],["study in peace","tinch o‘qimoq"]],"wc":182},{"n":14,"q":"Some people prefer watching films at the cinema, while others prefer watching them at home. What are the advantages and disadvantages?","kind":"Advantages / disadvantages","title":"Cinema vs home","essay":["Nowadays, people can enjoy films both in cinemas and on streaming platforms. While the cinema offers an unforgettable atmosphere, I believe that watching films at home is the better choice.","There are several benefits of going to the cinema, one of which is the «immersive experience». Because the screen is huge and the sound is powerful, viewers feel part of the story. This often makes the film more exciting, thereby creating lasting memories. For example, an action film with loud explosions is far more thrilling on a big screen than on a laptop.","However, I believe that watching films at home is better, mainly because it is «cheaper and more comfortable». By streaming a film, a family of four avoids expensive tickets and snacks. As a result, they can watch more films every month. Viewers can also «pause the film» whenever they want. For instance, a mother can stop the movie to put her child to bed and continue later without missing anything.","In conclusion, although the cinema offers a special atmosphere, I firmly believe that watching films at home is the better choice because it is cheaper, flexible and comfortable."],"chunks":[["an immersive experience","to‘liq sho‘ng‘ish tajribasi"],["a huge screen","ulkan ekran"],["powerful sound","kuchli tovush"],["feel part of the story","o‘zini voqeaning bir qismi his qilmoq"],["create lasting memories","esda qoladigan xotiralar yaratmoq"],["a thrilling experience","hayajonli tajriba"],["special effects","maxsus effektlar"],["a shared experience","birgalikdagi tajriba"],["go on a date","uchrashuvga bormoq"],["expensive tickets","qimmat chiptalar"],["overpriced snacks","haddan tashqari qimmat gazaklar"],["cheaper and more comfortable","arzonroq va qulayroq"],["stream a film","filmni onlayn ko‘rmoq"],["pause the film","filmni to‘xtatib qo‘ymoq"],["watch at one’s own pace","o‘z sur’atida ko‘rmoq"],["a wide selection of films","filmlarning keng tanlovi"],["subscription service","obuna xizmati"],["travel to the cinema","kinoteatrga qatnamoq"],["fix a time","vaqtni belgilamoq"],["noisy audience","shovqinli tomoshabinlar"],["annoying behaviour","bezovta qiladigan xatti-harakat"],["relax on the sofa","divanda dam olmoq"],["invite friends over","do‘stlarni uyga taklif qilmoq"],["watch with subtitles","subtitr bilan ko‘rmoq"],["rewatch favourite scenes","sevimli sahnalarni qayta ko‘rmoq"],["save money on tickets","chiptalarda pulni tejamoq"],["a cosy atmosphere","shinam muhit"],["the big-screen experience","katta ekran tajribasi"],["new releases","yangi chiqqan filmlar"],["miss part of the film","filmning bir qismini o‘tkazib yubormoq"]],"wc":191},{"n":15,"q":"Some people believe protecting the environment is the responsibility of governments, while others think individuals should act. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Environment: governments or individuals","essay":["In recent times, environmental problems have become a serious concern worldwide. While individuals can do a lot through their daily habits, I believe that governments bear the main responsibility.","There are several reasons why individuals should act, one of which is that their daily habits «add up». When millions of people «recycle waste» and save energy, the total effect on the planet is huge. This also sets a good example for children, thereby creating «environmentally responsible citizens». For example, a family that uses public transport instead of a car reduces air pollution every day.","However, I am convinced that governments carry the main responsibility, mainly because only they can «pass and enforce laws». By «imposing fines» on polluting factories and investing in clean energy, authorities achieve changes that individuals cannot. As a result, whole industries become greener, which benefits everyone. For instance, a law that bans plastic bags immediately reduces waste in every shop in the country.","In conclusion, although individual actions are valuable, I firmly believe that governments should lead environmental protection because they have the power to change entire systems."],"chun