 that arts subjects are essential, mainly because they «develop creativity». By acting in plays or playing instruments, children learn to «express their feelings» and think in original ways. As a result, they become more confident, which also helps them in other subjects. Arts lessons also reduce stress. For instance, a shy pupil who joins the school choir may gain the courage to speak in front of the class.","In conclusion, although arts lessons take time from core subjects, I firmly believe that every school should teach them because they develop creativity and confidence."],"chunks":[["arts subjects","san’at fanlari"],["drama and music","drama va musiqa"],["core subjects","asosiy fanlar"],["take time away from","...dan vaqt olib qo‘ymoq"],["limited hours","cheklangan soatlar"],["cover the syllabus","dasturni qamrab olmoq"],["lower exam results","imtihon natijalarining pasayishi"],["disappoint parents","ota-onalarni xafa qilmoq"],["focus on academic subjects","akademik fanlarga e’tibor qaratmoq"],["develop creativity","ijodkorlikni rivojlantirmoq"],["express one’s feelings","his-tuyg‘ularini ifodalamoq"],["think in original ways","original fikrlamoq"],["play an instrument","cholg‘u asbobida chalmoq"],["act in a play","spektaklda o‘ynamoq"],["become more confident","ishonchliroq bo‘lmoq"],["gain the courage","jasorat to‘plamoq"],["speak in public","omma oldida so‘zlamoq"],["join the school choir","maktab xoriga qo‘shilmoq"],["reduce stress","stressni kamaytirmoq"],["improve concentration","diqqatni yaxshilamoq"],["boost self-esteem","o‘ziga bo‘lgan hurmatni oshirmoq"],["discover hidden talents","yashirin iste’dodlarni kashf etmoq"],["well-rounded education","har tomonlama ta’lim"],["appreciate culture","madaniyatni qadrlamoq"],["encourage teamwork","jamoaviy ishlashni rag‘batlantirmoq"],["a creative outlet","ijodiy ifoda yo‘li"],["pursue a career in the arts","san’atda karyera qilmoq"],["expensive equipment","qimmat jihozlar"],["improve memory","xotirani yaxshilamoq"],["a balanced curriculum","muvozanatli o‘quv dasturi"]],"wc":192},{"n":19,"q":"Some people say technology has made entertainment easier, while others believe it has made life more complicated. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Technology: entertainment easier or life complicated","essay":["The question of whether technology has simplified or complicated life is widely discussed. While too many choices can be confusing, I believe that technology has made entertainment easier.","There are several reasons why some people find technology complicated, one of which is that there are «too many choices». When streaming platforms offer thousands of films, viewers spend a long time «deciding what to watch». This often causes frustration, thereby reducing enjoyment. For example, a family may argue for half an hour about which series to start.","However, I am convinced that technology has made entertainment easier, mainly because it provides «instant access» to almost anything. By using a phone or a tablet, people can watch films, listen to music or play games anywhere. As a result, they can relax during a long journey or a short break. Technology also lowers costs. For instance, a monthly subscription gives unlimited music for the price of a single CD.","In conclusion, although too many options can be confusing, I firmly believe that technology has made entertainment easier because it is fast, cheap and available everywhere."],"chunks":[["too many choices","juda ko‘p tanlov"],["streaming platforms","striming platformalari"],["decide what to watch","nima ko‘rishni hal qilmoq"],["cause frustration","g‘ashni keltirmoq"],["reduce enjoyment","zavqni kamaytirmoq"],["argue about","... haqida bahslashmoq"],["information overload","axborot ortiqchaligi"],["feel overwhelmed","o‘zini bosim ostida his qilmoq"],["instant access","bir zumda kirish imkoni"],["watch films anywhere","istalgan joyda film ko‘rmoq"],["listen to music","musiqa tinglamoq"],["play games online","onlayn o‘yin o‘ynamoq"],["relax during a journey","yo‘lda dam olmoq"],["a short break","qisqa tanaffus"],["lower costs","xarajatlarni pasaytirmoq"],["monthly subscription","oylik obuna"],["unlimited music","cheksiz musiqa"],["on demand","talab bo‘yicha"],["personalised recommendations","shaxsiylashtirilgan tavsiyalar"],["a wide variety of content","kontentning keng xilma-xilligi"],["high-quality entertainment","yuqori sifatli ko‘ngilochar vositalar"],["virtual reality","virtual reallik"],["become addicted to","...ga qaram bo‘lib qolmoq"],["waste hours","soatlarni behuda sarflamoq"],["complicated settings","murakkab sozlamalar"],["technical problems","texnik muammolar"],["a slow connection","sekin ulanish"],["spend less time with family","oila bilan kamroq vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["keep up with technology","texnologiyaga ilgarilab borishni uddalamoq"],["simplify life","hayotni soddalashtirmoq"]],"wc":182},{"n":20,"q":"Some people believe swimming should be a compulsory subject at school. Do you agree?","kind":"Agree / disagree","title":"Compulsory swimming","essay":["Nowadays, there is a debate about whether swimming should be a compulsory school subject. While pools are expensive to build and run, I believe that swimming lessons should be compulsory.","There are several reasons why people oppose compulsory swimming, one of which is that it requires «expensive facilities». Because pools need heating, cleaning and trained instructors, many schools cannot afford them. This can lead to unequal opportunities, thereby frustrating pupils. For example, a rural school without a pool may need to hire buses to take children to a distant sports centre.","However, I am convinced that swimming should be compulsory, mainly because it is «a life-saving skill». By learning to swim, children can protect themselves and others near rivers, lakes and beaches. As a result, the number of drowning accidents falls, which saves lives every year. Swimming also «improves physical fitness». For instance, a child who swims twice a week builds strong muscles and a healthy heart without joining an expensive gym.","In conclusion, although swimming lessons require costly facilities, I firmly believe that they should be compulsory because they save lives and keep children healthy."],"chunks":[["a compulsory subject","majburiy fan"],["expensive facilities","qimmat inshootlar"],["heat a pool","basseynni isitmoq"],["trained instructors","tayyorgarlik ko‘rgan o‘qituvchilar"],["cannot afford","(narxini) ko‘tara olmaslik"],["unequal opportunities","teng bo‘lmagan imkoniyatlar"],["a rural school","qishloq maktabi"],["hire buses","avtobus ijaraga olmoq"],["a distant sports centre","uzoqdagi sport markazi"],["a life-saving skill","hayot saqlovchi ko‘nikma"],["protect oneself","o‘zini himoya qilmoq"],["near rivers and lakes","daryo va ko‘llar yaqinida"],["drowning accidents","cho‘kish hodisalari"],["save lives","jonlarni asramoq"],["improve physical fitness","jismoniy tayyorgarlikni yaxshilamoq"],["build strong muscles","baquvvat mushaklarni shakllantirmoq"],["a healthy heart","sog‘lom yurak"],["full-body exercise","butun tanaga mashq"],["low-impact exercise","tanaga yengil yuk beradigan mashq"],["reduce the risk of injury","jarohat xavfini kamaytirmoq"],["develop confidence in water","suvda ishonchni rivojlantirmoq"],["fear of water","suvdan qo‘rqish"],["teach water safety","suv xavfsizligini o‘rgatmoq"],["a lifelong skill","umrbod ko‘nikma"],["team sports","jamoaviy sport turlari"],["promote an active lifestyle","faol turmush tarzini targ‘ib qilmoq"],["rise in obesity","semizlikning ko‘payishi"],["a lack of time","vaqt yetishmasligi"],["a crowded timetable","band dars jadvali"],["a fun activity","qiziqarli mashg‘ulot"]],"wc":186},{"n":21,"q":"Some people think live performances such as theatre are better than films. What are the advantages and disadvantages?","kind":"Advantages / disadvantages","title":"Live performances vs films","essay":["In recent times, streaming has made films more popular than ever, yet many people still love live theatre. While live performances have a unique atmosphere, I believe that their high cost and inconvenience are serious drawbacks.","There are several advantages of live theatre, one of which is the «unique atmosphere». When actors perform in front of an audience, every show is slightly different and full of energy. This often creates a strong emotional connection, thereby making the experience unforgettable. For example, an audience member who watches a tragic scene a few metres away may feel the emotion much more deeply than on a screen.","However, I believe that live performances also have serious disadvantages, mainly because they are «expensive and inconvenient». By buying tickets, travelling to the city and arriving on time, spectators spend a great deal of money and effort. As a result, many families can only go once a year, whereas films can be watched at any time. For instance, a student on a small budget can stream a film for a few dollars, but a theatre ticket may cost ten times more.","In conclusion, although live performances offer a unique atmosphere, I firmly believe that their high cost and inconvenience make them less accessible than films."],"chunks":[["live performance","jonli ijro"],["a unique atmosphere","noyob muhit"],["full of energy","energiyaga to‘la"],["in front of an audience","tomoshabinlar oldida"],["a strong emotional connection","kuchli hissiy aloqa"],["make the experience unforgettable","tajribani unutilmas qilmoq"],["a tragic scene","fojiali sahna"],["feel the emotion deeply","hissiyotni chuqur his qilmoq"],["interact with the audience","tomoshabinlar bilan muloqot qilmoq"],["talented actors","iste’dodli aktyorlar"],["stage design","sahna bezagi"],["a cultural event","madaniy tadbir"],["expensive and inconvenient","qimmat va noqulay"],["buy tickets","chipta sotib olmoq"],["travel to the city","shaharga borib kelmoq"],["arrive on time","o‘z vaqtida yetib kelmoq"],["spend a great deal of money","ko‘p pul sarflamoq"],["a small budget","kichik byudjet"],["stream a film","filmni onlayn ko‘rmoq"],["watch at any time","istalgan vaqtda ko‘rmoq"],["limited performances","cheklangan namoyishlar"],["sold-out shows","chiptalari sotilib bo‘lgan shoular"],["miss the show","shouni o‘tkazib yubormoq"],["cannot be repeated","takrorlab bo‘lmaydi"],["special effects","maxsus effektlar"],["a wide audience","keng tomoshabinlar auditoriyasi"],["affordable entertainment","hamyonbop ko‘ngilochar vosita"],["support the arts","san’atni qo‘llab-quvvatlamoq"],["a night out","oqshom tashqarida o‘tkazish"],["live music","jonli musiqa"]],"wc":209},{"n":22,"q":"Some people believe young people spend too much time on screens. What problems does this cause, and how can it be solved?","kind":"Problem / solution","title":"Too much screen time","essay":["Nowadays, young people spend a large part of their day looking at screens. While screens make learning and entertainment easier, I believe that this habit causes serious problems that parents and schools can solve.","There are several problems caused by excessive screen time, one of which is the damage to «physical health». When young people sit in front of a screen for hours, they become inactive and often «suffer from eye strain» and poor posture. This can lead to weight gain, thereby increasing the risk of serious illnesses. For example, a teenager who plays video games every evening may rarely do any exercise.","To solve this problem, parents should «set clear limits» on daily screen use. By agreeing a time schedule and encouraging outdoor hobbies, they can help children develop a healthier lifestyle. As a result, young people sleep better and concentrate more easily at school. Schools can also organise sports clubs. For instance, a boy who joins a football team after lessons will spend less time on his phone.","In conclusion, although screens have many benefits, I firmly believe that clear rules at home and more physical activities can reduce the problems of excessive screen time."],"chunks":[["spend too much time on screens","ekranlarda juda ko‘p vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["physical health","jismoniy salomatlik"],["sit in front of a screen","ekran oldida o‘tirmoq"],["become inactive","harakatsiz bo‘lib qolmoq"],["suffer from eye strain","ko‘z charchog‘idan aziyat chekmoq"],["poor posture","noto‘g‘ri qad-qomat"],["gain weight","vazn ortirmoq"],["increase the risk of illness","kasallik xavfini oshirmoq"],["do exercise","jismoniy mashq qilmoq"],["play video games","video o‘yin o‘ynamoq"],["set clear limits","aniq chegaralar belgilamoq"],["agree a time schedule","vaqt jadvalini kelishib olmoq"],["encourage outdoor hobbies","ochiq havodagi hobbilarni rag‘batlantirmoq"],["develop a healthier lifestyle","sog‘lomroq turmush tarzini shakllantirmoq"],["sleep better","yaxshiroq uxlamoq"],["concentrate at school","maktabda diqqatni jamlamoq"],["disturb sleep","uyquni buzmoq"],["shorten attention span","diqqat davomiyligini qisqartirmoq"],["spend less time with family","oila bilan kamroq vaqt o‘tkazmoq"],["face-to-face communication","yuzma-yuz muloqot"],["become addicted","qaramlikka tushmoq"],["parental controls","ota-ona nazorati"],["screen-free time","ekransiz vaqt"],["organise sports clubs","sport to‘garaklari tashkil etmoq"],["promote active hobbies","faol hobbilarni targ‘ib qilmoq"],["lead by example","o‘rnak bo‘lmoq"],["educate children about risks","bolalarni xavflar haqida o‘qitmoq"],["limit screen time","ekran vaqtini cheklamoq"],["switch off devices","qurilmalarni o‘chirmoq"],["poor academic results","yomon o‘zlashtirish natijalari"]],"wc":197},{"n":23,"q":"Some people believe online courses are as effective as classroom lessons. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Online courses vs classroom lessons","essay":["In recent times, online courses have become increasingly popular all over the world. While they offer great flexibility, I believe that classroom lessons are more effective.","There are several reasons why people support online courses, one of which is their «flexibility». When students can study at any time and place, they can «combine their studies with work». This often reduces stress, thereby helping them stay motivated. For example, a mother with young children can watch lectures after they fall asleep.","However, I am convinced that classroom lessons are more effective, mainly because they offer «face-to-face interaction». By asking questions and receiving immediate feedback, learners solve problems quickly. As a result, they understand difficult topics better, which improves their results. Classrooms also keep students disciplined. For instance, a learner who must attend lessons every morning is less likely to postpone his studies than one who studies alone at home.","In conclusion, although online courses are flexible, I firmly believe that classroom lessons are more effective because they provide direct support and discipline."],"chunks":[["online courses","onlayn kurslar"],["classroom lessons","sinfdagi darslar"],["study at any time and place","istalgan vaqt va joyda o‘qimoq"],["combine studies with work","o‘qish va ishni birlashtirmoq"],["stay motivated","motivatsiyani saqlab qolmoq"],["watch lectures","ma’ruzalarni tomosha qilmoq"],["a flexible schedule","moslashuvchan jadval"],["save travel time","yo‘l vaqtini tejamoq"],["lower tuition fees","pastroq o‘qish to‘lovi"],["access to experts","mutaxassislarga murojaat imkoni"],["face-to-face interaction","yuzma-yuz muloqot"],["ask questions","savol bermoq"],["receive immediate feedback","darhol fikr-mulohaza olmoq"],["solve problems quickly","muammolarni tez hal qilmoq"],["understand difficult topics","qiyin mavzularni tushunmoq"],["improve results","natijalarni yaxshilamoq"],["stay disciplined","intizomli bo‘lib qolmoq"],["postpone studies","o‘qishni keyinga qoldirmoq"],["lack of self-discipline","o‘zini tutish yetishmasligi"],["get distracted easily","osongina chalg‘ib ketmoq"],["technical problems","texnik muammolar"],["a poor internet connection","yomon internet aloqasi"],["feel isolated","o‘zini ajralgan his qilmoq"],["a sense of community","jamoa hissi"],["group discussions","guruh muhokamalari"],["hands-on practice","amaliy mashg‘ulot"],["a structured timetable","tizimli dars jadvali"],["a motivating atmosphere","rag‘batlantiruvchi muhit"],["drop out of a course","kursni tashlab ketmoq"],["receive a certificate","sertifikat olmoq"]],"wc":171},{"n":24,"q":"Some people say companies should train their employees, while others believe employees should develop their own skills. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Company training vs own skills","essay":["The question of who should be responsible for developing workers’ skills is often discussed. While employees can improve themselves, I believe that companies should provide training.","There are several reasons why employees should develop their own skills, one of which is that it «shows initiative». When workers take online courses in their free time, they prepare themselves for «career advancement». This often makes them more valuable, thereby increasing their chances of promotion. For example, an accountant who learns data analysis independently may become a manager faster.","However, I am convinced that companies should provide training, mainly because it «improves overall performance». By teaching staff the latest methods and software, employers ensure that everyone works efficiently. As a result, mistakes decrease, which saves money. Training also increases loyalty. For instance, a worker whose company pays for a course may stay for many years instead of looking for a new job.","In conclusion, although personal development is important, I firmly believe that companies should train their employees because it benefits both the staff and the business."],"chunks":[["train employees","xodimlarni o‘qitmoq"],["develop one’s own skills","o‘z ko‘nikmalarini rivojlantirmoq"],["show initiative","tashabbus ko‘rsatmoq"],["take online courses","onlayn kurslar olmoq"],["in one’s free time","bo‘sh vaqtida"],["career advancement","karyera o‘sishi"],["increase the chances of promotion","lavozim ko‘tarilish imkoniyatini oshirmoq"],["become more valuable","qimmatliroq bo‘lmoq"],["learn independently","mustaqil o‘rganmoq"],["improve overall performance","umumiy samaradorlikni yaxshilamoq"],["the latest methods","eng so‘nggi usullar"],["up-to-date software","zamonaviy dasturiy ta’minot"],["work efficiently","samarali ishlamoq"],["decrease mistakes","xatolarni kamaytirmoq"],["save money","pulni tejamoq"],["increase loyalty","sadoqatni oshirmoq"],["pay for a course","kurs uchun pul to‘lamoq"],["stay with a company","kompaniyada qolmoq"],["look for a new job","yangi ish qidirmoq"],["on-the-job training","ish joyida o‘qitish"],["specific company needs","kompaniyaning aniq ehtiyojlari"],["a skilled workforce","malakali ishchi kuchi"],["keep up with change","o‘zgarishlarga hamqadam bo‘lmoq"],["take responsibility","mas’uliyatni zimmasiga olmoq"],["lifelong learning","umrbod ta’lim"],["waste time and money","vaqt va pulni isrof qilmoq"],["reduce staff turnover","xodimlar almashinuvini kamaytirmoq"],["boost morale","ruhiy holatni ko‘tarmoq"],["gain new qualifications","yangi malakalar olmoq"],["stay competitive","raqobatbardosh bo‘lib qolmoq"]],"wc":174},{"n":25,"q":"Some people believe all students should do volunteer work. What are the advantages and disadvantages?","kind":"Advantages / disadvantages","title":"Compulsory volunteer work","essay":["Nowadays, some schools consider making volunteer work compulsory for all students. While volunteering has clear benefits, I believe that its disadvantages outweigh them when it is forced.","There are several benefits of compulsory volunteering, one of which is that it teaches «a sense of responsibility». When students help in hospitals or shelters, they learn to care about others and «give something back to society». This often builds their confidence, thereby preparing them for adult life. For example, a pupil who helps elderly neighbours with shopping may become more patient and mature.","However, I believe that the disadvantages are more serious, mainly because forcing students to volunteer can «cause resentment». By adding unpaid work to their busy timetable, schools may increase stress before exams. As a result, pupils may do the tasks carelessly, which defeats the purpose. For instance, a teenager who must spend every Saturday at a charity may feel exhausted and lose interest in helping.","In conclusion, although volunteering has clear benefits, I firmly believe that its disadvantages outweigh them when it is compulsory, and students should be encouraged rather than forced."],"chunks":[["do volunteer work","ko‘ngilli ish bilan shug‘ullanmoq"],["compulsory volunteering","majburiy ko‘ngillilik"],["a sense of responsibility","mas’uliyat hissi"],["care about others","boshqalarga g‘amxo‘rlik qilmoq"],["give something back to society","jamiyatga o‘z hissasini qaytarmoq"],["build confidence","ishonchni shakllantirmoq"],["prepare for adult life","katta hayotga tayyorlamoq"],["help elderly neighbours","keksa qo‘shnilarga yordam bermoq"],["become more mature","yetukroq bo‘lmoq"],["learn patience","sabrni o‘rganmoq"],["gain work experience","ish tajribasi orttirmoq"],["improve a CV","rezyumeni yaxshilamoq"],["develop empathy","hamdardlikni rivojlantirmoq"],["work in shelters","boshpanalarda ishlamoq"],["support local charities","mahalliy xayriya tashkilotlarini qo‘llab-quvvatlamoq"],["cause resentment","norozilikni keltirib chiqarmoq"],["a busy timetable","band jadval"],["unpaid work","haq to‘lanmaydigan ish"],["increase stress","stressni oshirmoq"],["do tasks carelessly","vazifalarni e’tiborsiz bajarmoq"],["defeat the purpose","maqsadni yo‘qqa chiqarmoq"],["feel exhausted","o‘zini horg‘in his qilmoq"],["lose interest","qiziqishni yo‘qotmoq"],["a genuine desire to help","yordam berishga chin istak"],["a personal choice","shaxsiy tanlov"],["force students","o‘quvchilarni majburlamoq"],["take time away from studies","o‘qishdan vaqt olmoq"],["encourage participation","ishtirokni rag‘batlantirmoq"],["strengthen communities","jamoalarni mustahkamlamoq"],["make a positive difference","ijobiy o‘zgarish qilmoq"]],"wc":183},{"n":26,"q":"Some people believe working from home is better than working in an office, while others disagree. What is your opinion?","kind":"Opinion","title":"Working from home vs office","essay":["In recent times, working from home has become common in many professions. While office work supports teamwork, I believe that working from home is the better option.","There are several reasons why some employers prefer office work, one of which is that teamwork may suffer when people work remotely. When colleagues are in different places, «spontaneous conversations disappear» and misunderstandings occur more often. This can slow down projects, thereby frustrating managers and customers. For example, a designer who cannot quickly ask a developer a question may wait hours for an email reply.","However, I am convinced that working from home is better, mainly because it helps employees «save money and time». By skipping the daily commute, staff no longer pay for fuel or tickets and gain extra hours. As a result, they can spend more time with their families, which reduces stress. For instance, someone who travels two hours a day can use that time for exercise and rest.","In conclusion, although office work supports teamwork, I firmly believe that working from home is better because it saves time and money and improves work-life balance."],"chunks":[["work from home","uydan ishlamoq"],["work remotely","masofadan ishlamoq"],["teamwork may suffer","jamoaviy ish zarar ko‘rishi mumkin"],["spontaneous conversations","o‘z-o‘zidan bo‘ladigan suhbatlar"],["misunderstandings occur","tushunmovchiliklar yuzaga keladi"],["slow down projects",