usted and long for fresh air. Housing is also costly. For instance, a family may pay half of their income for a small flat, whereas a countryside house is much cheaper.","In conclusion, although big cities offer many opportunities, I firmly believe that their noise, pollution and high costs make the countryside a better place to live."],"chunks":[["a wide range of job opportunities","ish imkoniyatlarining keng tanlovi"],["large companies","yirik kompaniyalar"],["further one’s education","ta’limni davom ettirmoq"],["higher salaries","yuqoriroq maoshlar"],["improve the standard of living","turmush darajasini yaxshilamoq"],["a capital city","poytaxt"],["modern facilities","zamonaviy inshootlar"],["a vibrant social life","jonli ijtimoiy hayot"],["cultural attractions","madaniy diqqatga sazovor joylar"],["access to healthcare","tibbiy xizmatdan foydalanish imkoni"],["public transport","jamoat transporti"],["noisy and polluted","shovqinli va ifloslangan"],["exhaust fumes","chiqindi gazlar"],["constant traffic","doimiy tirbandlik"],["suffer from stress","stressdan aziyat chekmoq"],["long for fresh air","toza havoga zor bo‘lmoq"],["a costly flat","qimmat kvartira"],["pay half of one’s income","daromadining yarmini to‘lamoq"],["a high cost of living","yuqori yashash narxi"],["overcrowded streets","gavjum ko‘chalar"],["a fast pace of life","hayot sur’atining tezligi"],["a peaceful lifestyle","tinch turmush tarzi"],["a close-knit community","o‘zaro yaqin jamoa"],["a lack of services","xizmatlar yetishmasligi"],["limited job opportunities","cheklangan ish imkoniyatlari"],["a safe environment","xavfsiz muhit"],["clean air","toza havo"],["a lower crime rate","jinoyatchilikning pastroq darajasi"],["spacious homes","keng uylar"],["rural areas","qishloq hududlari"]],"wc":189},{"n":30,"q":"Some people say that people today buy far more things than they really need. What problems does this cause, and how can it be solved?","kind":"Problem / solution","title":"Buying more than we need","essay":["Nowadays, shops and online platforms make it easy to buy almost anything at any time. While shopping can be enjoyable, I believe that buying more than we need creates problems that careful planning can solve.","There are several problems caused by excessive buying, one of which is «financial stress». When people spend on unnecessary items, they often «run out of money» before the end of the month. This can lead to debt, thereby damaging their well-being. For example, a young worker who buys the latest phone every year may struggle to pay rent.","To solve this problem, people should «plan their spending» carefully. By writing a shopping list and waiting a few days before big purchases, they can avoid impulse buying. As a result, they save money, which reduces financial worry. Governments and schools can also teach «financial literacy». For instance, a pupil who learns to budget at school is more likely to spend wisely as an adult.","In conclusion, although shopping brings pleasure, I firmly believe that careful planning and financial education can reduce the problem of buying more than we need."],"chunks":[["buy more than one needs","keraklidan ortiq xarid qilmoq"],["unnecessary items","keraksiz narsalar"],["financial stress","moliyaviy stress"],["run out of money","pulsiz qolmoq"],["fall into debt","qarzga botmoq"],["damage well-being","farovonlikka zarar yetkazmoq"],["struggle to pay rent","ijara haqini to‘lashda qiynalmoq"],["buy the latest phone","eng yangi telefonni sotib olmoq"],["plan one’s spending","xarajatlarini rejalashtirmoq"],["write a shopping list","xaridlar ro‘yxatini yozmoq"],["avoid impulse buying","o‘ylamay xarid qilishdan qochmoq"],["save money","pul jamg‘armoq"],["reduce financial worry","moliyaviy xavotirni kamaytirmoq"],["teach financial literacy","moliyaviy savodxonlikni o‘rgatmoq"],["learn to budget","byudjet tuzishni o‘rganmoq"],["spend wisely","oqilona sarflamoq"],["a consumer society","iste’molchilik jamiyati"],["advertising pressure","reklama bosimi"],["special offers","maxsus takliflar"],["attractive discounts","jozibador chegirmalar"],["follow fashion trends","moda tendensiyalariga ergashmoq"],["show off wealth","boyligini ko‘rsatmoq"],["a throwaway culture","“ishlat-tashla” madaniyati"],["create waste","chiqindi hosil qilmoq"],["overflowing landfills","to‘lib ketgan chiqindixonalar"],["waste natural resources","tabiiy resurslarni isrof qilmoq"],["buy second-hand","ishlatilgan narsalarni sotib olmoq"],["repair rather than replace","almashtirish o‘rniga ta’mirlamoq"],["live within one’s means","daromadiga qarab yashamoq"],["a minimalist lifestyle","minimalist turmush tarzi"]],"wc":183}];
